var tipuesearch = {"pages":[{"title":" rotlib ","text":"rotlib Developer Info Sarit Dutta","tags":"home","url":"index.html"},{"title":"mat_is_rotmat – rotlib","text":"public  function mat_is_rotmat(mat, tol) Returns .true. if a (3,3) matrix is a rotation matrix, .false. otherwise. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: mat (3,3) . Matrix to check. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Absolute tolerance for comparing determinant and orthogonality. Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"proc/mat_is_rotmat.html"},{"title":"quat_is_normalized – rotlib","text":"public  function quat_is_normalized(q, tol) Returns .true. if a quaternion is normalized, i.e. if it is a unit\nquaternion, within a tolerance tol ; .false. otherwise. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q A quaternion real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Absolute allowable deviation of the norm from one. Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_is_normalized.html"},{"title":"quat_angle_between – rotlib","text":"public  function quat_angle_between(p, q) result(angle) Returns the smallest rotation angle between the orientations represented\nby two unit quaternions. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: p Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. Return Value real(kind=rp) Relative rotation angle in radians, in the interval [0, pi] . \nOpposite-sign quaternions representing the same orientation have\nzero separation","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_angle_between.html"},{"title":"mat_is_dcm – rotlib","text":"public  function mat_is_dcm(mat, tol) Checks if mat is a direction cosine matrix or not. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: mat Matrix to check. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Absolute tolerance for comparing determinant and orthogonality. Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"proc/mat_is_dcm.html"},{"title":"align – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine align(v, old, new, valigned) Rotate vectors such that a set of at most three mutually orthogonal unit\nvectors aligns with another set of mutually orthogonal unit vectors. The\ntwo sets of mutually orthogonal unit vectors must contain the same number\nof unit vectors. v , old , and new store their constituent vectors column-wise, with\nall vectors resolved in the same fixed underlying basis. The vectors in v are rotated using a rotation matrix R such that new(:,i) = R @ old(:,i) , for each unit vector i (stored in the i th column), with the single vector ( n=1 ) case treated equivalently.\nHere @ represents matrix multiplication. If old is a single vector, a unique rotation cannot be defined. In this\ncase, the shortest rotation mapping old to new is chosen. For\nanti-parallel directions, this is a half-turn about a chosen axis\nperpendicular to old . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,m) . Vectors to align. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: old (3,n) . A set of at most three mutually orthogonal unit vectors. n must be one of 1, 2 or 3. If n = 3 , the three unit vectors\nmust form a right-handed basis. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: new (3,n) . Another set of mutually orthogonal unit vectors of the same\nshape as old . If n = 3 , the three unit vectors must form a right-handed\nbasis. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: valigned (3,m) . Aligned vectors, of the same shape as v . The components in out are resolved in the same underlying basis as the vectors in v .","tags":"","url":"proc/align.html"},{"title":"quat_canonicalized – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_canonicalized(q) Modifies a non-canonical unit quaternion in-place to bring it to the\ncanonical form. No modifications are performed if the input is already in canonical form. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a unit quaternion. If q is not in canonical form,\non return, q is modified to bring it to the canonical form, \nelse q is left as is.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_canonicalized.html"},{"title":"quat_rand – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_rand(q) Draws a unit quaternion from a uniform distribution on the space of\nrotations in 3D. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion in canonical form.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_rand.html"},{"title":"quat_identity – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_identity(q) Returns the identity unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_identity.html"},{"title":"quat_conjugated – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_conjugated(q) Conjugates a quaternion in-place. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a quaternion. On return, the conjugated quaternion.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_conjugated.html"},{"title":"quat_inverted – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_inverted(q, estat) Inverts a quaternion in-place. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a quaternion. On return, the inverted quaternion. integer, intent(out), optional :: estat Error code. Equals 1 for a zero-quaternion, else 0 .","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_inverted.html"},{"title":"quat_normalized – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_normalized(q, canonicalize, estat) Normalizes a quaternion in-place. In case of a zero quaternion, q is not changed and an error code of 1 is returned. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a quaternion. On return, the normalized quaternion\n(in canonical form if canonicalize is .true. ). logical, intent(in), optional :: canonicalize Whether to canonicalize the output. integer, intent(out), optional :: estat Error code. Returns 1 for a zero quaternion, else 0.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_normalized.html"},{"title":"quat_prod – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_prod(p, q, pq) Calculates the product of two quaternions following Hamilton's\nconvention. In case of unit quaternions describing rotations in a\ncommon frame, q 's rotation is applied first, followed by that of p . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: p Quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: pq Product of p and q .","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_prod.html"},{"title":"quat_interpolate – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_interpolate(q1, q2, t, q) Performs spherical linear interpolation between two unit quaternions\nfollowing the shortest path. The second endpoint may be negated to select the shortest path. At a relative orientation (physical) of exactly pi , two equally short\npaths exist; the supplied endpoint signs determine which is selected. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q1 Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q2 Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: t A fraction between 0 and 1 (both inclusive) specifying the\ninterpolation point. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Interpolated unit quaternion.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_interpolate.html"},{"title":"quat_deriv_to_angvel_mat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_deriv_to_angvel_mat(q, world, mat) Returns the matrix mapping the derivative of a unit quaternion to\nangular velocity. Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an\nactive rotation in A by a unit quaternion q aligns its basis vectors\nwith those of frame B.  Then the matrix M returned is such that omega_i =\nM_ij * qdot_j , where omega_i is the angular velocity of B relative to\nA resolved in A (or B) and qdot_j is the time derivative of q . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world\nframe), else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,4) :: mat Angular velocity matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_deriv_to_angvel_mat.html"},{"title":"quat_deriv_to_angvel – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_deriv_to_angvel(q, qdot, world, angvel) Calculates the angular velocity from a unit quaternion and its time\nderivative. Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an\nactive rotation in A by a unit quaternion q aligns its basis vectors\nwith those of frame B. Let qdot be the time derivative of q . The\nquantity returned is the angular velocity of B relative to A resolved in A\n(or B). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: qdot Time derivative of q . In general, this is not a unit vector.\nNote that qdot is orthogonal to q , i.e. q . qdot = 0 . logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world frame),\nelse, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: angvel Angular velocity.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_deriv_to_angvel.html"},{"title":"quat_deriv_from_angvel_mat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_deriv_from_angvel_mat(q, world, mat) Returns the matrix mapping angular velocity to time derivative of a \nunit quaternion. Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an\nactive rotation in A by a unit quaternion q aligns its basis vectors\nwith those of frame B. Then the matrix M returned is such that qdot_i =\nM_ij * omega_j , where omega_j is the angular velocity of B relative\nto A resolved in A (or B) and qdot_i is the time derivative of q . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world\nframe), else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4,3) :: mat Quaternion derivative matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_deriv_from_angvel_mat.html"},{"title":"quat_deriv_from_angvel – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_deriv_from_angvel(q, angvel, world, qdot) Calculates the time derivative of a unit quaternion from angular velocity. Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an\nactive rotation in A by a unit quaternion q aligns its basis vectors\nwith those of frame B. Let angvel be the angular velocity of B\nrelative to A resolved in A (or B). The quantity returned is the time\nderivative of q . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. An active rotation of frame A by q aligns it with\nframe B. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: angvel Angular velocity of frame B relative to frame A resolved in A if world=.true. , or in B otherwise. logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world frame),\nelse, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: qdot Time derivative of q . It is orthogonal to q and not a unit vector in\ngeneral.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_deriv_from_angvel.html"},{"title":"quat_rotmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_rotmat(q, rotmat) Returns the rotation matrix corresponding to a unit quaternion. For a column vector v of length 3, the rotated vector v' = R v , where R is the returned matrix.  The components of v and v' are\nexpressed in the same fixed orthonormal basis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_rotmat.html"},{"title":"quat_shiftmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_shiftmat(q, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to a unit quaternion. The orientation of frame B relative to frame A is specified by a unit\nquaternion q , such that an active rotation in A of its basis vectors\naligns them with those of B. The shifter matrix S transforms the\ncomponents of a fixed vector resolved in A to those resolved in B or\nvice-versa according to v_B_i = S_ij * v_A_j or v_A_i = S_ij *\nv_B_j . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_shiftmat.html"},{"title":"quat_rotate_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_rotate_vectors(v, q, vrot) Rotates vectors by a unit quaternion. The components of v and the \nrotated vectors are all expressed in the same fixed basis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Vectors to rotate, stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) Rotated vectors.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_rotate_vectors.html"},{"title":"quat_shift_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_shift_vectors(v, q, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by a unit quaternion q .\nThis orientation is used for both transformation directions.  The vectors\nremain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of forward . logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v .","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_shift_vectors.html"},{"title":"quat_shift_tensor2 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_shift_tensor2(a, q, forward, ashift) Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by a unit quaternion q .\nThis orientation is used for both transformation directions.  The tensor\nremains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a different frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Components of a second-order tensor.  Expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of forward . logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the same second-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_shift_tensor2.html"},{"title":"quat_shift_tensor3 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_shift_tensor3(a, q, forward, ashift) Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by a unit quaternion q .\nThis orientation is used for both transformation directions.  The tensor\nremains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a different frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a Components of a third-order tensor.  Expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of forward . logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the same third-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_shift_tensor3.html"},{"title":"quat_to_aa – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_to_aa(q, axis, angle) Converts a unit quaternion to an axis-angle representation. An\nidentity quaternion will return [1,0,0] as the axis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis of rotation. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle in radian (lies in [0, pi] ).","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_to_aa.html"},{"title":"quat_to_dcm – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_to_dcm(q, dcm) Converts a unit quaternion to a direction cosine matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_to_dcm.html"},{"title":"quat_to_euler – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine quat_to_euler(q, seq, world, tol, euler) Converts a unit quaternion to an Euler angle sequence. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles.","tags":"","url":"proc/quat_to_euler.html"},{"title":"aa_fix – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_fix(axis, angle, normalize_axis, estat) For a given orientation in axis-angle representation, returns a\nmodified axis and angle to ensure that angle lies in [0, pi] while preserving the rotation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(3) :: axis Axis of rotation. On entry, must be a non-zero vector. On return,\nif normalize_axis=.true. , the normalized axis . \nIf normalize_axis=.false. , it has the same magnitude as axis and may need to be normalized before using other axis-angle functions. real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: angle On entry, angle in radian. On return, modified angle in radian\nwithin [0, pi] . logical, intent(in) :: normalize_axis Whether to normalize the axis to a unit vector. integer, intent(out) :: estat Error code. Equals 1 if axis is a zero vector, else 0 .","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_fix.html"},{"title":"aa_rand – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_rand(axis, angle) Generates a random orientation in axis-angle representation drawn from\na uniform distribution on the space of rotations in 3D. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_rand.html"},{"title":"aa_rotmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_rotmat(axis, angle, rotmat) Returns the matrix for an active rotation about axis through angle ,\nwith positive angles following the right-hand rule. For a column vector v of length 3, the rotated vector v' = R v , where R is the returned matrix. The components of v , v' , and axis are\nexpressed in the same fixed orthonormal basis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand\nrule. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_rotmat.html"},{"title":"aa_from_rotmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_from_rotmat(rotmat, axis, angle) Extracts axis and angle from a rotation matrix.\nIf rotmat is an identity matrix, the axis returned is [1,0,0]. If the\nangle is exactly pi , either sign of the axis is valid. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix (must be orthonormal with determinant equal to one). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian within [0, pi] .","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_from_rotmat.html"},{"title":"aa_rotate_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_rotate_vectors(v, axis, angle, vrot) Rotates vectors about axis by angle . The components of axis , v , and the rotated vectors are all\nexpressed in the same fixed basis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Vectors to rotate stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand\nrule. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) . Rotated vectors.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_rotate_vectors.html"},{"title":"aa_shiftmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_shiftmat(axis, angle, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to an axis-angle representation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand\nrule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_shiftmat.html"},{"title":"aa_shift_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_shift_vectors(v, axis, angle, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by axis and angle ,\nwith axis expressed in A and positive angles following the right-hand\nrule. This orientation is used for both transformation directions.\nThe vectors remain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a\ndifferent frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of a vectors stored as columns. Expressed in\nA if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of forward real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians.\nPositive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) . Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v .","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_shift_vectors.html"},{"title":"aa_shift_tensor2 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_shift_tensor2(a, axis, angle, forward, ashift) Transforms second-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by axis and angle ,\nwith axis expressed in A and positive angles following the right-hand\nrule. This orientation is used for both transformation directions.\nThe tensor remains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a\ndifferent frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Components of a second-order tensor, expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of forward real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians.\nPositive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the second-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_shift_tensor2.html"},{"title":"aa_shift_tensor3 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_shift_tensor3(a, axis, angle, forward, ashift) Transforms third-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by axis and angle ,\nwith axis expressed in A and positive angles following the right-hand\nrule. This orientation is used for both transformation directions.\nThe tensor remains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a\ndifferent frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a Components of a third-order tensor, expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of forward real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians.\nPositive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the third-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_shift_tensor3.html"},{"title":"aa_to_quat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_to_quat(axis, angle, q) Converts an axis-angle representation to a unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion in the canonical form.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_to_quat.html"},{"title":"aa_to_dcm – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_to_dcm(axis, angle, dcm) Converts an axis-angle representation to a direction cosine matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along  the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_to_dcm.html"},{"title":"aa_to_euler – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine aa_to_euler(axis, angle, seq, world, tol, euler) Coverts an axis-angle representation to Euler angles . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle in radian. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles.","tags":"","url":"proc/aa_to_euler.html"},{"title":"dcm_from_frames – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_from_frames(A, B, dcm) Returns the direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A,\nwhere the bases of the frames are resolved in an underlying fixed frame F.\nIf F coincides with A, then A reduces to an identity matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: A The columns of A represent the orthonormal basis vectors of a\nright-handed frame A resolved in F. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: B The columns of B represent the orthonormal basis vectors of a\nright-handed frame B resolved in F. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_from_frames.html"},{"title":"dcm_rotmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_rotmat(dcm, rotmat) Returns the rotation matrix corresponding to a direction cosine matrix. Let D be the direction cosine matrix of frame B relative to frame A.  The\nrotation matrix R corresponding to D rotates vectors resolved in A such\nthat the bases of A align with those of B, when all the bases are resolved\nin A. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_rotmat.html"},{"title":"dcm_shiftmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_shiftmat(dcm, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to a direction cosine matrix. Let D be the direction cosine matrix of frame B relative to frame A. The\nshifter matrix S corresponding to D transforms components of vectors (or\ntensors) resolved in A to those in B (or vice-versa). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_shiftmat.html"},{"title":"dcm_rotate_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_rotate_vectors(v, dcm, vrot) Rotates vectors by a direction cosine matrix. Let D be the direction cosine matrix of frame B relative to frame A.\nVectors resolved in A are rotated such that the bases of A align with those\nof B, when all the bases are resolved in A. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of a single vector or n vectors stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) . Rotated vectors.","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_rotate_vectors.html"},{"title":"dcm_shift_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_shift_vectors(v, dcm, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by dcm . This orientation\nis used for both transformation directions. The vectors remain unchanged;\nonly their components are expressed in a different frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed\nin A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) . Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v .","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_shift_vectors.html"},{"title":"dcm_shift_tensor2 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_shift_tensor2(a, dcm, forward, ashift) Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by dcm . This orientation\nis used for both transformation directions. The tensor remains unchanged;\nonly its components are expressed in a different frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a A second-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_shift_tensor2.html"},{"title":"dcm_shift_tensor3 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_shift_tensor3(a, dcm, forward, ashift) Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by dcm . This orientation\nis used for both transformation directions. The tensor remains unchanged;\nonly its components are expressed in a different frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a A third-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_shift_tensor3.html"},{"title":"dcm_to_quat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_to_quat(dcm, q) Converts a direction cosine matrix to a unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion.","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_to_quat.html"},{"title":"dcm_to_aa – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_to_aa(dcm, axis, angle) Converts a direction cosine matrix to an axis-angle representation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle in radian (lies in [0, pi] ).","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_to_aa.html"},{"title":"dcm_to_euler – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine dcm_to_euler(dcm, seq, world, tol, euler) Converts a direction cosine matrix to Euler angles. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles","tags":"","url":"proc/dcm_to_euler.html"},{"title":"euler_rotmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_rotmat(euler, seq, world, rotmat) Returns the rotation matrix for a set of Euler angles. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_rotmat.html"},{"title":"euler_shiftmat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_shiftmat(euler, seq, world, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix for a set of Euler angles. The orientation of frame B relative to frame A is specified by a set of\nEuler angles. The shifter matrix S transforms components of vectors (or\ntensors) resolved in A to those in B (or vice-versa). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_shiftmat.html"},{"title":"euler_rotate_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_rotate_vectors(v, euler, seq, world, vrot) Rotates vectors with a set of Euler angles. The components of v and the rotated vectors are all expressed in the same fixed basis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) . Rotated vectors.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_rotate_vectors.html"},{"title":"euler_shift_vectors – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_shift_vectors(v, euler, seq, world, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by Euler angles.\nThis orientation is used for both transformation directions. The vectors\nremain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different\nframe. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed\nin A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) . Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v .","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_shift_vectors.html"},{"title":"euler_shift_tensor2 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_shift_tensor2(a, euler, seq, world, forward, ashift) Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by Euler angles.\nThis orientation is used for both transformation directions. The vectors\nremain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different\nframe. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a A second-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_shift_tensor2.html"},{"title":"euler_shift_tensor3 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_shift_tensor3(a, euler, seq, world, forward, ashift) Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. The orientation of B relative to A is specified by Euler angles.\nThis orientation is used for both transformation directions. The vectors\nremain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different\nframe. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a A third-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_shift_tensor3.html"},{"title":"euler_to_quat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_to_quat(euler, seq, world, q) Convert Euler angles to a unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion in canonical form.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_to_quat.html"},{"title":"euler_to_aa – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_to_aa(euler, seq, world, axis, angle) Convert Euler angles to an axis-angle representation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis of rotation. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian (lies in [0, pi] ).","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_to_aa.html"},{"title":"euler_to_dcm – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_to_dcm(euler, seq, world, dcm) Convert Euler angles to a direction cosine matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_to_dcm.html"},{"title":"euler_to_euler – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine euler_to_euler(euler, seq, world, to_seq, to_world, tol, to_euler) Convert one set of Euler angles to another. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nSequence for euler . logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. character(len=3), intent(in) :: to_seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nConvert euler with sequence seq to the sequence to_seq . logical, intent(in) :: to_world Whether the converted euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: to_euler Converted Euler angles.","tags":"","url":"proc/euler_to_euler.html"},{"title":"isclose – rotlib","text":"public elemental function isclose(a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two floating point numbers of type double are close within\ntolerance. Based on python implementation at https://github.com/PythonCHB/close_pep/blob/master/is_close.py .\nThe method='weak' option is used here. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance, rel_tol >= 0 , default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance, abs_tol >= 0 , default 0.0 Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"proc/isclose.html"},{"title":"allclose_rank1 – rotlib","text":"public  function allclose_rank1(a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-1 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: a (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: b (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"proc/allclose_rank1.html"},{"title":"allclose_rank2 – rotlib","text":"public  function allclose_rank2(a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-2 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: a (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: b (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"proc/allclose_rank2.html"},{"title":"allclose_rank3 – rotlib","text":"public  function allclose_rank3(a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-3 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: a (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: b (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"proc/allclose_rank3.html"},{"title":"sinc – rotlib","text":"public elemental function sinc(x) result(res) Calculates sin(x)/x elementwise. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: x Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/sinc.html"},{"title":"norm – rotlib","text":"public  function norm(v) result(res) Calculates the 2-norm of a vector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/norm.html"},{"title":"vec_angle_3d – rotlib","text":"public  function vec_angle_3d(a, b) result(res) Returns the angle (in radian) between two non-zero vectors in 3D. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/vec_angle_3d.html"},{"title":"uvec_angle – rotlib","text":"public  function uvec_angle(u, v) result(res) Returns the angle (in radian) between two unit vectors using Kahan's half\nangle formula. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: u Unit vector real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v Unit vector Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/uvec_angle.html"},{"title":"scalar_triple_product – rotlib","text":"public  function scalar_triple_product(a, b, c) result(res) Returns the scalar triple product a .( b x c ) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: c Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/scalar_triple_product.html"},{"title":"det – rotlib","text":"public  function det(A) result(res) Returns the determinant of an (N x N) matrix, where N = 2, 3, or 4. Original routine by David Simpson Note For a general NxN matrix do an LU decomp Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: A (N,N) array, where N = 2, 3, or 4. Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/det.html"},{"title":"trace – rotlib","text":"public  function trace(mat) result(res) Returns the trace of a square matrix Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: mat (:,:) (N,N) array Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/trace.html"},{"title":"get_quad_form – rotlib","text":"public  function get_quad_form(A, x) result(res) Calculates the quadratic form x&#94;T A x , where A is an n x n matrix and x is a\nvector of length n Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: A (n,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x (n,) array Return Value real(kind=rp)","tags":"","url":"proc/get_quad_form.html"},{"title":"swap_integer – rotlib","text":"public elemental subroutine swap_integer(a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(inout) :: a integer, intent(inout) :: b","tags":"","url":"proc/swap_integer.html"},{"title":"swap_real – rotlib","text":"public elemental subroutine swap_real(a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b","tags":"","url":"proc/swap_real.html"},{"title":"swap_complex – rotlib","text":"public elemental subroutine swap_complex(a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b","tags":"","url":"proc/swap_complex.html"},{"title":"rad2deg – rotlib","text":"public elemental subroutine rad2deg(rad, deg) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: rad real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: deg","tags":"","url":"proc/rad2deg.html"},{"title":"deg2rad – rotlib","text":"public elemental subroutine deg2rad(deg, rad) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: deg real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: rad","tags":"","url":"proc/deg2rad.html"},{"title":"normalized – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine normalized(v, estat) Normalizes a vector in-place. If the magnitude of the vector is zero, \nthe vector is not modified and an optional error status of 1 is returned. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: v A vector integer, intent(out), optional :: estat Error status. Equals 1 in case of a zero vector, and 0 otherwise.","tags":"","url":"proc/normalized.html"},{"title":"cross – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine cross(a, b, c) Calculates the cross product between two 3-element vectors. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: c Cross product of a and b ; c = a x b","tags":"","url":"proc/cross.html"},{"title":"cross_mat – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine cross_mat(a, mat) Calculates the cross product matrix of a 3-element vector. The cross\nproduct matrix A of a is defined as a x b = A . b ,\nwhere b is another 3-element vector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: mat Cross product matrix of a","tags":"","url":"proc/cross_mat.html"},{"title":"vector_triple_product – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine vector_triple_product(a, b, c, d) Returns the vector triple product d = a x ( b x c ) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: c real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: d Vector triple product","tags":"","url":"proc/vector_triple_product.html"},{"title":"outer – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine outer(a, b, c) Calculates the outer product of two vectors, . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: a (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: b (n,) array real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: c (m,n) array; Outer product","tags":"","url":"proc/outer.html"},{"title":"linspace – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine linspace(start, finish, num, val, step) Generates evenly spaced numbers over a specified interval. Both end\npoints are included. If start > finish , the returned step size (if step is present) will be negative. Values are interpolated directly from the endpoints to avoid overflow\nin the endpoint difference. Floating-point rounding can make adjacent\nspacings unequal or produce repeated values. The supplied endpoints\nare assigned exactly. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: start Finite starting point real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: finish Finite ending point, finish /= start integer, intent(in) :: num Number of values to generate, num >= 2 real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: val (n,) array, where n >= num . Generated values. Elements beyond\nthe first num values are left as is. real(kind=rp), intent(out), optional :: step Nominal step size, which may differ from adjacent output spacings\nbecause of rounding. For num=2 , its calculation can overflow if\nthe endpoint difference is not representable. No step is calculated\nwhen this argument is absent.","tags":"","url":"proc/linspace.html"},{"title":"logspace – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine logspace(start, finish, num, val, base) Generates numbers spaced evenly on a log scale.\nIn linear space, the sequence starts at base ** start ( base to the power of start ) and ends with base ** finish Exponents are generated by linspace . Floating-point rounding can\nmake adjacent ratios unequal or produce repeated values. The endpoint\npowers are subject to rounding, overflow, and underflow as well. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: start Finite starting exponent; base ** start is the starting value real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: finish Finite ending exponent, finish /= start ; base ** finish is the ending value integer, intent(in) :: num Number of values to generate, num >= 2 real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: val (n,) array, where n >= num . Generated values. Elements beyond\nthe first num values are left as is. real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: base Base of the logspace. Must be finite and positive, default is 10.","tags":"","url":"proc/logspace.html"},{"title":"identity – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine identity(mat_eye) Creates an identity matrix of size n x n. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: mat_eye (n,n) array","tags":"","url":"proc/identity.html"},{"title":"get_diagonal – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine get_diagonal(mat, d) Returns the diagonal elements of a square matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: mat (n,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: d (n,) array; contains the entries of the main diagonal","tags":"","url":"proc/get_diagonal.html"},{"title":"add_transpose – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine add_transpose(mat) Adds a square matrix and its transpose in place: Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: mat (n,n) array","tags":"","url":"proc/add_transpose.html"},{"title":"subtract_transpose – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine subtract_transpose(mat) Calculates the difference of a square matrix and its transpose in place: Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: mat","tags":"","url":"proc/subtract_transpose.html"},{"title":"multiply_transpose – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine multiply_transpose(A, B) Multiplies a matrix with its transpose: Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: A (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: B (m,m) array","tags":"","url":"proc/multiply_transpose.html"},{"title":"orth_mgs – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine orth_mgs(a, estat) Orthogonalizes a set of non-zero vectors in-place using modified\nGram-Schmidt orthonormalization. Reference: Golub and Van Loan, Matrix Computations, 4th edition,\nSection 5.2.8, Algorithm 5.2.6, p. 255. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: a (m,n) rank n array, where m >= n , storing the vectors\ncolumn-wise. On return, the columns of the matrix are overwritten\nwith the orthogonal vectors. integer, intent(out) :: estat Error code. Returns 1 if during execution a column is found to be\nzero, 0 otherwise. A return with estat=1 may leave a partially\noverwritten.","tags":"","url":"proc/orth_mgs.html"},{"title":"invert_mat33 – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine invert_mat33(a, inv_a) Inverts a 3x3 matrix with non-zero determinant. Reference: https://www.geometrictools.com/Documentation/LaplaceExpansionTheorem.pdf Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Matrix real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: inv_a Matrix inverse","tags":"","url":"proc/invert_mat33.html"},{"title":"eigval_33rsym – rotlib","text":"public  subroutine eigval_33rsym(a, ev) Calculates the eigenvalues of a finite real symmetric 3 x 3 matrix,\nin decreasing order. The input matrix is not modified. Uses maximum-entry scaling and Jacobi rotations to avoid overflow in\nintermediate products and cancellation in cubic-equation formulas near\nrepeated eigenvalues. Diagonal matrices are handled directly.\nIteration stops when the largest off-diagonal entry is at most machine\nepsilon times the largest absolute diagonal entry of the scaled matrix. Accuracy is relative to the matrix scale; high relative accuracy for\nvery small eigenvalues or very small eigenvalue gaps is not guaranteed.\nRescaling can overflow if an eigenvalue is outside the range of rp ,\nor underflow if it is too small to represent. Reference: J. Kopp, Efficient numerical diagonalization of Hermitian\n3 x 3 matrices, https://arxiv.org/abs/physics/0610206 Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Finite symmetric input matrix. Both triangles must be supplied. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: ev Eigenvalues, with ev(1) >= ev(2) >= ev(3) .","tags":"","url":"proc/eigval_33rsym.html"},{"title":"allclose – rotlib","text":"public interface allclose Checks if two arrays are elementwise close within tolerance Module Procedures public  function allclose_rank1 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-1 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: a (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: b (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public  function allclose_rank2 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-2 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: a (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: b (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public  function allclose_rank3 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-3 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: a (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: b (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface/allclose.html"},{"title":"swap – rotlib","text":"public interface swap Swaps two arrays Module Procedures public elemental subroutine swap_integer (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(inout) :: a integer, intent(inout) :: b public elemental subroutine swap_real (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b public elemental subroutine swap_complex (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b","tags":"","url":"interface/swap.html"},{"title":"constants_m – rotlib","text":"Predefined constants, including math constants. Uses iso_fortran_env Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: ip = int32 Default integer precision integer, public, parameter :: ip_long = int64 Default long integer precision integer, public, parameter :: rp = real64 Default real precision integer, public, parameter :: sizeof_char = 1 Size of a char in bytes integer, public, parameter :: sizeof_int = 4 Size of a default int in bytes integer, public, parameter :: sizeof_long_int = 8 Size of a default long int in bytes integer, public, parameter :: sizeof_real = 8 Size of a default real in bytes real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_third = 0.333333333333333_rp One third : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_pi = 3.1415926535897931_rp pi : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_pi_2 = 1.5707963267948966_rp pi/2 : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_pi_4 = 0.78539816339744828_rp pi/4 : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_1_pi = 0.31830988618379069_rp Reciprocal of pi : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_2_pi = 0.63661977236758138_rp Two times reciprocal of pi : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_2_sqrtpi = 1.1283791670955126_rp Two times the reciprocal of the square root of pi : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_sqrt2 = 1.4142135623730951_rp Square root of two : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_cbrt2 = 1.2599210498948732_rp Cube root of two : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_sqrt1_2 = 0.70710678118654746_rp Reciprocal of the square root of two : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_sqrt3 = 1.7320508075688772_rp Square root of three : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_sqrt_e = 1.6487212707001282_rp Square root of e : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_sqrt_pi = 1.7724538509055159_rp Square root of pi : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_e = 2.7182818284590451_rp The base of natural logarithm : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_log2e = 1.4426950408889634_rp The logarithm of e to base two : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_log10e = 0.43429448190325182_rp The logarithm of e to base 10 : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_ln2 = 0.69314718055994529_rp The natural logarithm of two : real(kind=rp), public, parameter :: math_ln10 = 2.3025850929940459_rp The natural logarithm of 10 :","tags":"","url":"module/constants_m.html"},{"title":"rotlib_m – rotlib","text":"Uses constants_m utils_math_m Functions public  function mat_is_rotmat (mat, tol) Returns .true. if a (3,3) matrix is a rotation matrix, .false. otherwise. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: mat (3,3) . Matrix to check. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Absolute tolerance for comparing determinant and orthogonality. Return Value logical public  function quat_is_normalized (q, tol) Returns .true. if a quaternion is normalized, i.e. if it is a unit\nquaternion, within a tolerance tol ; .false. otherwise. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q A quaternion real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Absolute allowable deviation of the norm from one. Return Value logical public  function quat_angle_between (p, q) result(angle) Returns the smallest rotation angle between the orientations represented\nby two unit quaternions. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: p Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. Return Value real(kind=rp) Relative rotation angle in radians, in the interval [0, pi] . \nOpposite-sign quaternions representing the same orientation have\nzero separation public  function mat_is_dcm (mat, tol) Checks if mat is a direction cosine matrix or not. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: mat Matrix to check. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Absolute tolerance for comparing determinant and orthogonality. Return Value logical Subroutines public  subroutine align (v, old, new, valigned) Rotate vectors such that a set of at most three mutually orthogonal unit\nvectors aligns with another set of mutually orthogonal unit vectors. The\ntwo sets of mutually orthogonal unit vectors must contain the same number\nof unit vectors. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,m) . Vectors to align. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: old (3,n) . A set of at most three mutually orthogonal unit vectors. n must be one of 1, 2 or 3. If n = 3 , the three unit vectors\nmust form a right-handed basis. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: new (3,n) . Another set of mutually orthogonal unit vectors of the same\nshape as old . If n = 3 , the three unit vectors must form a right-handed\nbasis. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: valigned (3,m) . Aligned vectors, of the same shape as v . The components in out are resolved in the same underlying basis as the vectors in v . public  subroutine quat_canonicalized (q) Modifies a non-canonical unit quaternion in-place to bring it to the\ncanonical form. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a unit quaternion. If q is not in canonical form,\non return, q is modified to bring it to the canonical form, \nelse q is left as is. public  subroutine quat_rand (q) Draws a unit quaternion from a uniform distribution on the space of\nrotations in 3D. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion in canonical form. public  subroutine quat_identity (q) Returns the identity unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. public  subroutine quat_conjugated (q) Conjugates a quaternion in-place. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a quaternion. On return, the conjugated quaternion. public  subroutine quat_inverted (q, estat) Inverts a quaternion in-place. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a quaternion. On return, the inverted quaternion. integer, intent(out), optional :: estat Error code. Equals 1 for a zero-quaternion, else 0 . public  subroutine quat_normalized (q, canonicalize, estat) Normalizes a quaternion in-place. In case of a zero quaternion, q is not changed and an error code of 1 is returned. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(4) :: q On entry, a quaternion. On return, the normalized quaternion\n(in canonical form if canonicalize is .true. ). logical, intent(in), optional :: canonicalize Whether to canonicalize the output. integer, intent(out), optional :: estat Error code. Returns 1 for a zero quaternion, else 0. public  subroutine quat_prod (p, q, pq) Calculates the product of two quaternions following Hamilton's\nconvention. In case of unit quaternions describing rotations in a\ncommon frame, q 's rotation is applied first, followed by that of p . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: p Quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: pq Product of p and q . public  subroutine quat_interpolate (q1, q2, t, q) Performs spherical linear interpolation between two unit quaternions\nfollowing the shortest path. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q1 Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q2 Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: t A fraction between 0 and 1 (both inclusive) specifying the\ninterpolation point. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Interpolated unit quaternion. public  subroutine quat_deriv_to_angvel_mat (q, world, mat) Returns the matrix mapping the derivative of a unit quaternion to\nangular velocity. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world\nframe), else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,4) :: mat Angular velocity matrix. public  subroutine quat_deriv_to_angvel (q, qdot, world, angvel) Calculates the angular velocity from a unit quaternion and its time\nderivative. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: qdot Time derivative of q . In general, this is not a unit vector.\nNote that qdot is orthogonal to q , i.e. q . qdot = 0 . logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world frame),\nelse, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: angvel Angular velocity. public  subroutine quat_deriv_from_angvel_mat (q, world, mat) Returns the matrix mapping angular velocity to time derivative of a \nunit quaternion. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world\nframe), else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4,3) :: mat Quaternion derivative matrix. public  subroutine quat_deriv_from_angvel (q, angvel, world, qdot) Calculates the time derivative of a unit quaternion from angular velocity. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. An active rotation of frame A by q aligns it with\nframe B. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: angvel Angular velocity of frame B relative to frame A resolved in A if world=.true. , or in B otherwise. logical, intent(in) :: world If .true. , the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world frame),\nelse, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: qdot Time derivative of q . It is orthogonal to q and not a unit vector in\ngeneral. public  subroutine quat_rotmat (q, rotmat) Returns the rotation matrix corresponding to a unit quaternion. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix. public  subroutine quat_shiftmat (q, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to a unit quaternion. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix. public  subroutine quat_rotate_vectors (v, q, vrot) Rotates vectors by a unit quaternion. The components of v and the \nrotated vectors are all expressed in the same fixed basis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Vectors to rotate, stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) Rotated vectors. public  subroutine quat_shift_vectors (v, q, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of forward . logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v . public  subroutine quat_shift_tensor2 (a, q, forward, ashift) Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Components of a second-order tensor.  Expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of forward . logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the same second-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine quat_shift_tensor3 (a, q, forward, ashift) Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a Components of a third-order tensor.  Expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of forward . logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the same third-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine quat_to_aa (q, axis, angle) Converts a unit quaternion to an axis-angle representation. An\nidentity quaternion will return [1,0,0] as the axis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis of rotation. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle in radian (lies in [0, pi] ). public  subroutine quat_to_dcm (q, dcm) Converts a unit quaternion to a direction cosine matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. public  subroutine quat_to_euler (q, seq, world, tol, euler) Converts a unit quaternion to an Euler angle sequence. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. public  subroutine aa_fix (axis, angle, normalize_axis, estat) For a given orientation in axis-angle representation, returns a\nmodified axis and angle to ensure that angle lies in [0, pi] while preserving the rotation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(3) :: axis Axis of rotation. On entry, must be a non-zero vector. On return,\nif normalize_axis=.true. , the normalized axis . \nIf normalize_axis=.false. , it has the same magnitude as axis and may need to be normalized before using other axis-angle functions. real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: angle On entry, angle in radian. On return, modified angle in radian\nwithin [0, pi] . logical, intent(in) :: normalize_axis Whether to normalize the axis to a unit vector. integer, intent(out) :: estat Error code. Equals 1 if axis is a zero vector, else 0 . public  subroutine aa_rand (axis, angle) Generates a random orientation in axis-angle representation drawn from\na uniform distribution on the space of rotations in 3D. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle public  subroutine aa_rotmat (axis, angle, rotmat) Returns the matrix for an active rotation about axis through angle ,\nwith positive angles following the right-hand rule. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand\nrule. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix. public  subroutine aa_from_rotmat (rotmat, axis, angle) Extracts axis and angle from a rotation matrix.\nIf rotmat is an identity matrix, the axis returned is [1,0,0]. If the\nangle is exactly pi , either sign of the axis is valid. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix (must be orthonormal with determinant equal to one). real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian within [0, pi] . public  subroutine aa_rotate_vectors (v, axis, angle, vrot) Rotates vectors about axis by angle . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Vectors to rotate stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand\nrule. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) . Rotated vectors. public  subroutine aa_shiftmat (axis, angle, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to an axis-angle representation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand\nrule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. , \ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix. public  subroutine aa_shift_vectors (v, axis, angle, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of a vectors stored as columns. Expressed in\nA if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of forward real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians.\nPositive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) . Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v . public  subroutine aa_shift_tensor2 (a, axis, angle, forward, ashift) Transforms second-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Components of a second-order tensor, expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of forward real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians.\nPositive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the second-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine aa_shift_tensor3 (a, axis, angle, forward, ashift) Transforms third-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a Components of a third-order tensor, expressed in A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of forward real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians.\nPositive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the third-order tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine aa_to_quat (axis, angle, q) Converts an axis-angle representation to a unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion in the canonical form. public  subroutine aa_to_dcm (axis, angle, dcm) Converts an axis-angle representation to a direction cosine matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along  the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. public  subroutine aa_to_euler (axis, angle, seq, world, tol, euler) Coverts an axis-angle representation to Euler angles . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: angle Angle in radian. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. public  subroutine dcm_from_frames (A, B, dcm) Returns the direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A,\nwhere the bases of the frames are resolved in an underlying fixed frame F.\nIf F coincides with A, then A reduces to an identity matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: A The columns of A represent the orthonormal basis vectors of a\nright-handed frame A resolved in F. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: B The columns of B represent the orthonormal basis vectors of a\nright-handed frame B resolved in F. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A public  subroutine dcm_rotmat (dcm, rotmat) Returns the rotation matrix corresponding to a direction cosine matrix. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix. public  subroutine dcm_shiftmat (dcm, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to a direction cosine matrix. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix. public  subroutine dcm_rotate_vectors (v, dcm, vrot) Rotates vectors by a direction cosine matrix. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of a single vector or n vectors stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) . Rotated vectors. public  subroutine dcm_shift_vectors (v, dcm, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed\nin A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) . Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v . public  subroutine dcm_shift_tensor2 (a, dcm, forward, ashift) Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a A second-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine dcm_shift_tensor3 (a, dcm, forward, ashift) Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a A third-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine dcm_to_quat (dcm, q) Converts a direction cosine matrix to a unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion. public  subroutine dcm_to_aa (dcm, axis, angle) Converts a direction cosine matrix to an axis-angle representation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle in radian (lies in [0, pi] ). public  subroutine dcm_to_euler (dcm, seq, world, tol, euler) Converts a direction cosine matrix to Euler angles. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles public  subroutine euler_rotmat (euler, seq, world, rotmat) Returns the rotation matrix for a set of Euler angles. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: rotmat Rotation matrix. public  subroutine euler_shiftmat (euler, seq, world, forward, shiftmat) Returns the shifter matrix for a set of Euler angles. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: shiftmat Shifter matrix. public  subroutine euler_rotate_vectors (v, euler, seq, world, vrot) Rotates vectors with a set of Euler angles. The components of v and the rotated vectors are all expressed in the same fixed basis. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vrot (3,n) . Rotated vectors. public  subroutine euler_shift_vectors (v, euler, seq, world, forward, vshift) Transform vector components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: v (3,n) . Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed\nin A if forward is .true. , or in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: vshift (3,n) . Components of the same vectors expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as v . public  subroutine euler_shift_tensor2 (a, euler, seq, world, forward, ashift) Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a A second-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine euler_shift_tensor3 (a, euler, seq, world, forward, ashift) Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3,3) :: a A third-order tensor, resolved in A if forward is .true. ,\nor in B otherwise. real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. logical, intent(in) :: forward If .true. , transform components from A to B. If .false. ,\ntransform components from B to A. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3,3) :: ashift Components of the same tensor expressed in B if forward is .true. , or in A otherwise. public  subroutine euler_to_quat (euler, seq, world, q) Convert Euler angles to a unit quaternion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(4) :: q Unit quaternion in canonical form. public  subroutine euler_to_aa (euler, seq, world, axis, angle) Convert Euler angles to an axis-angle representation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: axis Unit vector along the axis of rotation. real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: angle Angle of rotation in radian (lies in [0, pi] ). public  subroutine euler_to_dcm (euler, seq, world, dcm) Convert Euler angles to a direction cosine matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nEuler angle sequence. logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: dcm Direction cosine matrix. public  subroutine euler_to_euler (euler, seq, world, to_seq, to_world, tol, to_euler) Convert one set of Euler angles to another. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: euler Euler angles. character(len=3), intent(in) :: seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nSequence for euler . logical, intent(in) :: world Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. character(len=3), intent(in) :: to_seq 'XYZ' | 'XZY' | 'YXZ' | 'YZX' | 'ZXY' | 'ZYX' .\nConvert euler with sequence seq to the sequence to_seq . logical, intent(in) :: to_world Whether the converted euler angles are with respect to the world frame or not. real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: tol Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: to_euler Converted Euler angles.","tags":"","url":"module/rotlib_m.html"},{"title":"utils_math_m – rotlib","text":"Various utility functions, particularly for use with small matrices. Uses ieee_arithmetic constants_m Interfaces public        interface allclose Checks if two arrays are elementwise close within tolerance public  function allclose_rank1 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-1 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: a (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: b (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public  function allclose_rank2 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-2 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: a (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: b (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public  function allclose_rank3 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-3 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: a (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: b (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public        interface swap Swaps two arrays public elemental subroutine swap_integer (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(inout) :: a integer, intent(inout) :: b public elemental subroutine swap_real (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b public elemental subroutine swap_complex (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b Functions public elemental function isclose (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two floating point numbers of type double are close within\ntolerance. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance, rel_tol >= 0 , default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance, abs_tol >= 0 , default 0.0 Return Value logical public  function allclose_rank1 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-1 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: a (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: b (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public  function allclose_rank2 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-2 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: a (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: b (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public  function allclose_rank3 (a, b, rel_tol, abs_tol) Checks if two rank-3 floating point arrays of type double are close within\ntolerance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: a (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:,:) :: b (m,n,p) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: rel_tol Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: abs_tol Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 Return Value logical public elemental function sinc (x) result(res) Calculates sin(x)/x elementwise. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: x Return Value real(kind=rp) public  function norm (v) result(res) Calculates the 2-norm of a vector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v Return Value real(kind=rp) public  function vec_angle_3d (a, b) result(res) Returns the angle (in radian) between two non-zero vectors in 3D. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b Return Value real(kind=rp) public  function uvec_angle (u, v) result(res) Returns the angle (in radian) between two unit vectors using Kahan's half\nangle formula. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: u Unit vector real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: v Unit vector Return Value real(kind=rp) public  function scalar_triple_product (a, b, c) result(res) Returns the scalar triple product a .( b x c ) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: c Return Value real(kind=rp) public  function det (A) result(res) Returns the determinant of an (N x N) matrix, where N = 2, 3, or 4. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: A (N,N) array, where N = 2, 3, or 4. Return Value real(kind=rp) public  function trace (mat) result(res) Returns the trace of a square matrix Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: mat (:,:) (N,N) array Return Value real(kind=rp) public  function get_quad_form (A, x) result(res) Calculates the quadratic form x&#94;T A x , where A is an n x n matrix and x is a\nvector of length n Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: A (n,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x (n,) array Return Value real(kind=rp) Subroutines public elemental subroutine swap_integer (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(inout) :: a integer, intent(inout) :: b public elemental subroutine swap_real (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b public elemental subroutine swap_complex (a, b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: a complex(kind=rp), intent(inout) :: b public elemental subroutine rad2deg (rad, deg) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: rad real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: deg public elemental subroutine deg2rad (deg, rad) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: deg real(kind=rp), intent(out) :: rad public  subroutine normalized (v, estat) Normalizes a vector in-place. If the magnitude of the vector is zero, \nthe vector is not modified and an optional error status of 1 is returned. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: v A vector integer, intent(out), optional :: estat Error status. Equals 1 in case of a zero vector, and 0 otherwise. public  subroutine cross (a, b, c) Calculates the cross product between two 3-element vectors. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: c Cross product of a and b ; c = a x b public  subroutine cross_mat (a, mat) Calculates the cross product matrix of a 3-element vector. The cross\nproduct matrix A of a is defined as a x b = A . b ,\nwhere b is another 3-element vector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: mat Cross product matrix of a public  subroutine vector_triple_product (a, b, c, d) Returns the vector triple product d = a x ( b x c ) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: a real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: b real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: c real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: d Vector triple product public  subroutine outer (a, b, c) Calculates the outer product of two vectors, . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: a (m,) array real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: b (n,) array real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: c (m,n) array; Outer product public  subroutine linspace (start, finish, num, val, step) Generates evenly spaced numbers over a specified interval. Both end\npoints are included. If start > finish , the returned step size (if step is present) will be negative. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: start Finite starting point real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: finish Finite ending point, finish /= start integer, intent(in) :: num Number of values to generate, num >= 2 real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: val (n,) array, where n >= num . Generated values. Elements beyond\nthe first num values are left as is. real(kind=rp), intent(out), optional :: step Nominal step size, which may differ from adjacent output spacings\nbecause of rounding. For num=2 , its calculation can overflow if\nthe endpoint difference is not representable. No step is calculated\nwhen this argument is absent. public  subroutine logspace (start, finish, num, val, base) Generates numbers spaced evenly on a log scale.\nIn linear space, the sequence starts at base ** start ( base to the power of start ) and ends with base ** finish Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: start Finite starting exponent; base ** start is the starting value real(kind=rp), intent(in) :: finish Finite ending exponent, finish /= start ; base ** finish is the ending value integer, intent(in) :: num Number of values to generate, num >= 2 real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: val (n,) array, where n >= num . Generated values. Elements beyond\nthe first num values are left as is. real(kind=rp), intent(in), optional :: base Base of the logspace. Must be finite and positive, default is 10. public  subroutine identity (mat_eye) Creates an identity matrix of size n x n. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: mat_eye (n,n) array public  subroutine get_diagonal (mat, d) Returns the diagonal elements of a square matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: mat (n,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: d (n,) array; contains the entries of the main diagonal public  subroutine add_transpose (mat) Adds a square matrix and its transpose in place: Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: mat (n,n) array public  subroutine subtract_transpose (mat) Calculates the difference of a square matrix and its transpose in place: Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: mat public  subroutine multiply_transpose (A, B) Multiplies a matrix with its transpose: Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(:,:) :: A (m,n) array real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(:,:) :: B (m,m) array public  subroutine orth_mgs (a, estat) Orthogonalizes a set of non-zero vectors in-place using modified\nGram-Schmidt orthonormalization. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(inout), dimension(:,:) :: a (m,n) rank n array, where m >= n , storing the vectors\ncolumn-wise. On return, the columns of the matrix are overwritten\nwith the orthogonal vectors. integer, intent(out) :: estat Error code. Returns 1 if during execution a column is found to be\nzero, 0 otherwise. A return with estat=1 may leave a partially\noverwritten. public  subroutine invert_mat33 (a, inv_a) Inverts a 3x3 matrix with non-zero determinant. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Matrix real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3,3) :: inv_a Matrix inverse public  subroutine eigval_33rsym (a, ev) Calculates the eigenvalues of a finite real symmetric 3 x 3 matrix,\nin decreasing order. The input matrix is not modified. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=rp), intent(in), dimension(3,3) :: a Finite symmetric input matrix. Both triangles must be supplied. real(kind=rp), intent(out), dimension(3) :: ev Eigenvalues, with ev(1) >= ev(2) >= ev(3) .","tags":"","url":"module/utils_math_m.html"},{"title":"constants_m.f90 – rotlib","text":"Source Code !> Predefined constants, including math constants. ! TODO: Replace the names with equivalent macro names in glibc math.h ! module constants_m use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : int32 , int64 , real64 implicit none !> Default integer precision integer , parameter :: ip = int32 !> Default long integer precision integer , parameter :: ip_long = int64 !> Default real precision integer , parameter :: rp = real64 !> Size of a char in bytes integer , parameter :: sizeof_char = 1 !> Size of a default int in bytes integer , parameter :: sizeof_int = 4 !> Size of a default long int in bytes integer , parameter :: sizeof_long_int = 8 !> Size of a default real in bytes integer , parameter :: sizeof_real = 8 !> `One third` :  \\frac{1}{3}  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_third = 0.333333333333333_rp !> `pi` :  \\pi  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_pi = 3.1415926535897931_rp !> `pi/2` :  \\pi / 2  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_pi_2 = 1.5707963267948966_rp !> `pi/4` :  \\pi / 4  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_pi_4 = 0.78539816339744828_rp !> Reciprocal of `pi` :  1/\\pi  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_1_pi = 0.31830988618379069_rp !> Two times reciprocal of `pi` :  2/\\pi  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_2_pi = 0.63661977236758138_rp !>Two times the reciprocal of the square root of `pi` :  2/\\sqrt{\\pi}  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_2_sqrtpi = 1.1283791670955126_rp !>Square root of `two` : \\sqrt{2} real ( rp ), parameter :: math_sqrt2 = 1.4142135623730951_rp !>Cube root of `two` : \\sqrt[3]{2} real ( rp ), parameter :: math_cbrt2 = 1.2599210498948732_rp !>Reciprocal of the square root of two : 1/\\sqrt{2} real ( rp ), parameter :: math_sqrt1_2 = 0.70710678118654746_rp !>Square root of three : \\sqrt{3} real ( rp ), parameter :: math_sqrt3 = 1.7320508075688772_rp !>Square root of `e` : \\sqrt{e} real ( rp ), parameter :: math_sqrt_e = 1.6487212707001282_rp !>Square root of `pi` : \\sqrt{\\pi} real ( rp ), parameter :: math_sqrt_pi = 1.7724538509055159_rp !>The base of natural logarithm :  e  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_e = 2.7182818284590451_rp !>The logarithm of `e` to base two :  \\log_2 e  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_log2e = 1.4426950408889634_rp !>The logarithm of `e` to base 10 :  \\log_{10} e  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_log10e = 0.43429448190325182_rp !>The natural logarithm of two :  \\ln 2 real ( rp ), parameter :: math_ln2 = 0.69314718055994529_rp !>The natural logarithm of 10 :  \\ln 10  real ( rp ), parameter :: math_ln10 = 2.3025850929940459_rp end module constants_m","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/constants_m.f90.html"},{"title":"rotlib_m.f90 – rotlib","text":"Source Code module rotlib_m use constants_m , only : math_pi , math_pi_2 use utils_math_m implicit none public private :: factor_rotmat , shift_tensor2 , shift_tensor3 , & rotmat_xyz , rotmat_xzy , rotmat_yxz , & rotmat_yzx , rotmat_zxy , rotmat_zyx , & factor_rotmat_xyz , factor_rotmat_xzy , factor_rotmat_yxz , & factor_rotmat_yzx , factor_rotmat_zxy , factor_rotmat_zyx contains !*****************************************************************************! !                               UTILITY FUNCTIONS                             ! !*****************************************************************************! subroutine align ( v , old , new , valigned ) !! Rotate vectors such that a set of at most three mutually orthogonal unit !! vectors aligns with another set of mutually orthogonal unit vectors. The !! two sets of mutually orthogonal unit vectors must contain the same number !! of unit vectors. !! !! `v`, `old`, and `new` store their constituent vectors column-wise, with !! all vectors resolved in the same fixed underlying basis. !! !! The vectors in `v` are rotated using a rotation matrix `R` such that !! `new(:,i) = R @ old(:,i)`, for each unit vector `i` (stored in the !! `i` th column), with the single vector (`n=1`) case treated equivalently. !! Here `@` represents matrix multiplication. !! !! If `old` is a single vector, a unique rotation cannot be defined. In this !! case, the shortest rotation mapping `old` to `new` is chosen. For !! anti-parallel directions, this is a half-turn about a chosen axis !! perpendicular to `old`. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,m)`. Vectors to align. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: old !! `(3,n)`. A set of at most three mutually orthogonal unit vectors. !! `n` must be one of 1, 2 or 3. If `n = 3`, the three unit vectors !! must form a right-handed basis. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: new !! `(3,n)`. Another set of mutually orthogonal unit vectors of the same !! shape as `old`. If `n = 3`, the three unit vectors must form a right-handed !! basis. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: valigned !! `(3,m)`. Aligned vectors, of the same shape as `v`. The components in !! `out` are resolved in the same underlying basis as the vectors in `v`. real ( rp ) :: axis ( 3 ), vtmp ( 3 ), z_old ( 3 ), z_new ( 3 ), axes_old ( 3 , 3 ), & axes_new ( 3 , 3 ), mat ( 3 , 3 ) real ( rp ) :: cos_angle , sin_angle , angle integer :: n , estat , min_idx if ( any ( shape ( old ) /= shape ( new )) ) then write ( * , * ) 'Shape mismatch between `old` and `new`.' write ( * , * ) 'Shape of `old` = ' , shape ( old ) write ( * , * ) 'Shape of `new` = ' , shape ( new ) error stop end if n = size ( old , dim = 2 ) if ( n == 1 ) then ! Angle between old and new cos_angle = dot_product ( old (:, 1 ), new (:, 1 )) call cross ( old (:, 1 ), new (:, 1 ), axis ) sin_angle = norm ( axis ) !Always non-negative ! angle in [0, pi] as sin_angle > 0. angle = atan2 ( sin_angle , cos_angle ) ! try normalizing the axis call normalized ( axis , estat ) if ( estat == 0 ) then !Non-collinear vectors: standard case call aa_rotate_vectors ( v , axis , angle , valigned ) else !Collinear vectors: parallel or anti-parallel if ( cos_angle > 0.0_rp ) then !angle = 0; no rotation necessary valigned = v else !angle = pi: Rotation axis not unique. Pick a vector by !crossing old(:,1) with a cartesian direction least parallel !to it. !1. Find cartesian direction least parallel to old(:,1) min_idx = minloc ( abs ( old (:, 1 )), 1 ) !2. Create that basis vector vtmp = 0.0_rp vtmp ( min_idx ) = 1.0_rp !3. Cross old(:,1) with vtmp and unitize to get the rotation ! axis call cross ( old (:, 1 ), vtmp , axis ) !axis will always have +ve norm. call aa_fix ( axis , angle , . true ., estat ) !Rotate call aa_rotate_vectors ( v , axis , angle , valigned ) end if end if else if ( n == 2 ) then !The third vector orthogonal to `old` call cross ( old (:, 1 ), old (:, 2 ), z_old ) call normalized ( z_old , estat ) !The third vector orthogonal to `new` call cross ( new (:, 1 ), new (:, 2 ), z_new ) call normalized ( z_new , estat ) !The `old` and new `frames` axes_old (:, 1 : 2 ) = old ; axes_old (:, 3 ) = z_old axes_new (:, 1 : 2 ) = new ; axes_new (:, 3 ) = z_new mat = matmul ( axes_new , transpose ( axes_old )) valigned = matmul ( mat , v ) else if ( n == 3 ) then mat = matmul ( new , transpose ( old )) valigned = matmul ( mat , v ) end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ logical function mat_is_rotmat ( mat , tol ) !! Returns `.true.` if a `(3,3)` matrix is a rotation matrix, `.false.` !! otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: mat !! `(3,3)`. Matrix to check. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Absolute tolerance for comparing determinant and orthogonality. logical :: det_is_one , is_orthogonal real ( rp ) :: eye ( 3 , 3 ), mat_prod ( 3 , 3 ), det_mat call identity ( eye ) mat_prod = matmul ( mat , transpose ( mat )) det_mat = det ( mat ) det_is_one = abs ( det_mat - 1.0_rp ) <= tol is_orthogonal = maxval ( abs ( mat_prod - eye )) <= tol mat_is_rotmat = ( is_orthogonal . and . det_is_one ) end function !******************************************************************************! !                                  QUATERNION                                  ! !******************************************************************************! subroutine quat_canonicalized ( q ) !! Modifies a non-canonical unit quaternion in-place to bring it to the !! canonical form. !! !! No modifications are performed if the input is already in canonical form. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in out ) :: q !! On entry, a unit quaternion. If `q` is not in canonical form, !! on return, `q` is modified to bring it to the canonical form, !! else `q` is left as is. integer :: i do i = 1 , 4 if ( q ( i ) > 0.0_rp ) then return else if ( q ( i ) < 0.0_rp ) then q ( 1 ) = - q ( 1 ); q ( 2 ) = - q ( 2 ); q ( 3 ) = - q ( 3 ); q ( 4 ) = - q ( 4 ) return end if end do end subroutine !******************************************************************************! subroutine quat_rand ( q ) !! Draws a unit quaternion from a uniform distribution on the space of !! rotations in 3D. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: q !! Unit quaternion in canonical form. real ( rp ) :: u ( 3 ), sqrt_u1 , sqrt_1mu1 , cos_u2 , sin_u2 , cos_u3 , sin_u3 call random_number ( u ) sqrt_u1 = sqrt ( u ( 1 )) sqrt_1mu1 = sqrt ( 1.0 - u ( 1 )) cos_u2 = cos ( 2.0_rp * math_pi * u ( 2 )) sin_u2 = sin ( 2.0_rp * math_pi * u ( 2 )) cos_u3 = cos ( 2.0_rp * math_pi * u ( 3 )) sin_u3 = sin ( 2.0_rp * math_pi * u ( 3 )) q ( 1 ) = sqrt_1mu1 * cos_u2 q ( 2 ) = sqrt_1mu1 * sin_u2 q ( 3 ) = sqrt_u1 * sin_u3 q ( 4 ) = sqrt_u1 * cos_u3 call quat_canonicalized ( q ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_identity ( q ) !! Returns the identity unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. q ( 1 ) = 1.0_rp ; q ( 2 ) = 0.0_rp ; q ( 3 ) = 0.0_rp ; q ( 4 ) = 0.0_rp end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_conjugated ( q ) !! Conjugates a quaternion in-place. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in out ) :: q !! On entry, a quaternion. On return, the conjugated quaternion. q ( 2 : 4 ) = - q ( 2 : 4 ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_inverted ( q , estat ) !! Inverts a quaternion in-place. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in out ) :: q !! On entry, a quaternion. On return, the inverted quaternion. integer , intent ( out ), optional :: estat !! Error code. Equals `1` for a zero-quaternion, else `0`. real ( rp ) :: d , q_scaled ( 4 ), s if ( present ( estat )) estat = 0 s = maxval ( abs ( q )) if ( s == 0.0_rp ) then if ( present ( estat )) estat = 1 return else q_scaled = q / s d = dot_product ( q_scaled , q_scaled ) call quat_conjugated ( q_scaled ) q = ( q_scaled / d ) / s end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_normalized ( q , canonicalize , estat ) !! Normalizes a quaternion in-place. In case of a zero quaternion, !! `q` is not changed and an error code of `1` is returned. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in out ) :: q !! On entry, a quaternion. On return, the normalized quaternion !! (in canonical form if `canonicalize` is `.true.`). logical , intent ( in ), optional :: canonicalize !! Whether to canonicalize the output. integer , intent ( out ), optional :: estat !! Error code. Returns 1 for a zero quaternion, else 0. integer :: estat_ call normalized ( q , estat_ ) if ( estat_ == 1 ) then if ( present ( estat )) estat = estat_ return end if if ( present ( canonicalize )) then if ( canonicalize ) then call quat_canonicalized ( q ) end if end if if ( present ( estat )) estat = 0 end subroutine !************************************************************************ logical function quat_is_normalized ( q , tol ) !! Returns `.true.` if a quaternion is normalized, i.e. if it is a unit !! quaternion, within a tolerance `tol`; `.false.` otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! A quaternion real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Absolute allowable deviation of the norm from one. real ( rp ) :: nrm nrm = norm ( q ) quat_is_normalized = abs ( nrm - 1.0_rp ) <= tol end function !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_prod ( p , q , pq ) !! Calculates the product of two quaternions following Hamilton's !! convention. In case of unit quaternions describing rotations in a !! common frame, `q`'s rotation is applied first, followed by that of `p`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: p !! Quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: pq !! Product of `p` and `q`. pq ( 1 ) = p ( 1 ) * q ( 1 ) - p ( 2 ) * q ( 2 ) - p ( 3 ) * q ( 3 ) - p ( 4 ) * q ( 4 ) pq ( 2 ) = p ( 2 ) * q ( 1 ) + p ( 1 ) * q ( 2 ) - p ( 4 ) * q ( 3 ) + p ( 3 ) * q ( 4 ) pq ( 3 ) = p ( 3 ) * q ( 1 ) + p ( 4 ) * q ( 2 ) + p ( 1 ) * q ( 3 ) - p ( 2 ) * q ( 4 ) pq ( 4 ) = p ( 4 ) * q ( 1 ) - p ( 3 ) * q ( 2 ) + p ( 2 ) * q ( 3 ) + p ( 1 ) * q ( 4 ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ function quat_angle_between ( p , q ) result ( angle ) !! Returns the smallest rotation angle between the orientations represented !! by two unit quaternions. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: p !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ) :: angle !! Relative rotation angle in radians, in the interval `[0, pi]`. !! Opposite-sign quaternions representing the same orientation have !! zero separation real ( rp ) :: q_ ( 4 ), cos_angle , d_mag , s_mag q_ = q cos_angle = dot_product ( p , q_ ) if ( cos_angle < 0.0_rp ) then ! Negate q_ to ensure both p and q_ lie on the same hemisphere q_ = - q_ end if d_mag = norm ( p - q_ ) s_mag = norm ( p + q_ ) angle = 4.0_rp * atan2 ( d_mag , s_mag ) end function !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_interpolate ( q1 , q2 , t , q ) !! Performs spherical linear interpolation between two unit quaternions !! following the shortest path. !! !! The second endpoint may be negated to select the shortest path. !! !! At a relative orientation (physical) of exactly `pi`, two equally short !! paths exist; the supplied endpoint signs determine which is selected. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q1 !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q2 !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! A fraction between 0 and 1 (both inclusive) specifying the !! interpolation point. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: q !! Interpolated unit quaternion. real ( rp ) :: q2_ ( 4 ), cos_angle , d_mag , s_mag , theta , a , b , c q2_ = q2 cos_angle = dot_product ( q1 , q2_ ) if ( cos_angle < 0.0_rp ) then ! Negate q2_ to ensure both q1 and q2_ lie on the same hemisphere q2_ = - q2_ end if d_mag = norm ( q1 - q2_ ) s_mag = norm ( q1 + q2_ ) theta = 2.0_rp * atan2 ( d_mag , s_mag ) ! SLERP c = sinc ( theta ) a = ( 1.0_rp - t ) * sinc ( ( 1.0_rp - t ) * theta ) / c b = t * sinc ( t * theta ) / c q = a * q1 + b * q2_ call quat_normalized ( q , canonicalize = . false .) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_deriv_to_angvel_mat ( q , world , mat ) !! Returns the matrix mapping the derivative of a unit quaternion to !! angular velocity. !! !! Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an !! active rotation in A by a unit quaternion `q` aligns its basis vectors !! with those of frame B.  Then the matrix M returned is such that `omega_i = !! M_ij * qdot_j`, where `omega_i` is the angular velocity of B relative to !! A resolved in A (or B) and `qdot_j` is the time derivative of `q`. !! real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! If `.true.`, the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world !! frame), else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 4 ), intent ( out ) :: mat !! Angular velocity matrix. if ( world ) then mat = reshape ([ - q ( 2 ), - q ( 3 ), - q ( 4 ), & q ( 1 ), q ( 4 ), - q ( 3 ), & - q ( 4 ), q ( 1 ), q ( 2 ), & q ( 3 ), - q ( 2 ), q ( 1 ) ], [ 3 , 4 ]) else mat = reshape ([ - q ( 2 ), - q ( 3 ), - q ( 4 ), & q ( 1 ), - q ( 4 ), q ( 3 ), & q ( 4 ), q ( 1 ), - q ( 2 ), & - q ( 3 ), q ( 2 ), q ( 1 ) ], [ 3 , 4 ]) end if mat = 2.0_rp * mat end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_deriv_to_angvel ( q , qdot , world , angvel ) !! Calculates the angular velocity from a unit quaternion and its time !! derivative. !! !! Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an !! active rotation in A by a unit quaternion `q` aligns its basis vectors !! with those of frame B. Let `qdot` be the time derivative of `q`. The !! quantity returned is the angular velocity of B relative to A resolved in A !! (or B). real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: qdot !! Time derivative of `q`. In general, this is not a unit vector. !! Note that `qdot` is orthogonal to `q`, i.e. `q . qdot = 0`. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! If `.true.`, the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world frame), !! else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: angvel !! Angular velocity. real ( rp ) :: mat ( 3 , 4 ) call quat_deriv_to_angvel_mat ( q , world , mat ) angvel = matmul ( mat , qdot ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_deriv_from_angvel_mat ( q , world , mat ) !! Returns the matrix mapping angular velocity to time derivative of a !! unit quaternion. !! !! Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an !! active rotation in A by a unit quaternion `q` aligns its basis vectors !! with those of frame B. Then the matrix M returned is such that `qdot_i = !! M_ij * omega_j`, where `omega_j` is the angular velocity of B relative !! to A resolved in A (or B) and `qdot_i` is the time derivative of `q`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! If `.true.`, the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world !! frame), else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: mat !! Quaternion derivative matrix. if ( world ) then mat = reshape ([ - q ( 2 ), q ( 1 ), - q ( 4 ), q ( 3 ), & - q ( 3 ), q ( 4 ), q ( 1 ), - q ( 2 ), & - q ( 4 ), - q ( 3 ), q ( 2 ), q ( 1 )], [ 4 , 3 ]) else mat = reshape ([ - q ( 2 ), q ( 1 ), q ( 4 ), - q ( 3 ), & - q ( 3 ), - q ( 4 ), q ( 1 ), q ( 2 ), & - q ( 4 ), q ( 3 ), - q ( 2 ), q ( 1 )], [ 4 , 3 ]) end if mat = 0.5_rp * mat end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_deriv_from_angvel ( q , angvel , world , qdot ) !! Calculates the time derivative of a unit quaternion from angular velocity. !! !! Let A (world frame) and B (body frame) be reference frames such that an !! active rotation in A by a unit quaternion `q` aligns its basis vectors !! with those of frame B. Let `angvel` be the angular velocity of B !! relative to A resolved in A (or B). The quantity returned is the time !! derivative of `q`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. An active rotation of frame A by `q` aligns it with !! frame B. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: angvel !! Angular velocity of frame B relative to frame A resolved in A if !! `world=.true.`, or in B otherwise. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! If `.true.`, the angular velocity is resolved in frame A (world frame), !! else, it is resolved in frame B (body frame). real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: qdot !! Time derivative of `q`. It is orthogonal to `q` and not a unit vector in !! general. real ( rp ) :: mat ( 4 , 3 ) call quat_deriv_from_angvel_mat ( q , world , mat ) qdot = matmul ( mat , angvel ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_rotmat ( q , rotmat ) !! Returns the rotation matrix corresponding to a unit quaternion. !! !! For a column vector `v` of length 3, the rotated vector `v' = R v`, where !! `R` is the returned matrix.  The components of `v` and `v'` are !! expressed in the same fixed orthonormal basis. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat !! Rotation matrix. real ( rp ) :: q1sq , q2sq , q3sq , q4sq real ( rp ) :: q1q2 , q1q3 , q1q4 , q2q3 , q2q4 , q3q4 q1sq = q ( 1 ) * q ( 1 ) q2sq = q ( 2 ) * q ( 2 ) q3sq = q ( 3 ) * q ( 3 ) q4sq = q ( 4 ) * q ( 4 ) q1q2 = q ( 1 ) * q ( 2 ) q1q3 = q ( 1 ) * q ( 3 ) q1q4 = q ( 1 ) * q ( 4 ) q2q3 = q ( 2 ) * q ( 3 ) q2q4 = q ( 2 ) * q ( 4 ) q3q4 = q ( 3 ) * q ( 4 ) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q1sq + q2sq ) - 1.0_rp rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q2q3 + q1q4 ) rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q2q4 - q1q3 ) rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q2q3 - q1q4 ) rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q1sq + q3sq ) - 1.0_rp rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q3q4 + q1q2 ) rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q2q4 + q1q3 ) rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q3q4 - q1q2 ) rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = 2.0_rp * ( q1sq + q4sq ) - 1.0_rp end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_shiftmat ( q , forward , shiftmat ) !! Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to a unit quaternion. !! !! The orientation of frame B relative to frame A is specified by a unit !! quaternion `q`, such that an active rotation in A of its basis vectors !! aligns them with those of B. The shifter matrix `S` transforms the !! components of a fixed vector resolved in A to those resolved in B or !! vice-versa according to `v_B_i = S_ij * v_A_j` or `v_A_i = S_ij * !! v_B_j`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: shiftmat !! Shifter matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ) :: conj_q if ( forward ) then conj_q = q call quat_conjugated ( conj_q ) call quat_rotmat ( conj_q , shiftmat ) else call quat_rotmat ( q , shiftmat ) end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_rotate_vectors ( v , q , vrot ) !! Rotates vectors by a unit quaternion. The components of `v` and the !! rotated vectors are all expressed in the same fixed basis. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Vectors to rotate, stored as columns. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vrot !! `(3,n)` Rotated vectors. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call quat_rotmat ( q , rotmat ) vrot = matmul ( rotmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_shift_vectors ( v , q , forward , vshift ) !! Transform vector components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by a unit quaternion `q`. !! This orientation is used for both transformation directions.  The vectors !! remain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different frame. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed in A if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of `forward`. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vshift !! `(3,n)` Components of the same vectors expressed in B if `forward` !! is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as `v`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call quat_shiftmat ( q , forward , shiftmat ) vshift = matmul ( shiftmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_shift_tensor2 ( a , q , forward , ashift ) !! Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by a unit quaternion `q`. !! This orientation is used for both transformation directions.  The tensor !! remains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a different frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! Components of a second-order tensor.  Expressed in A if `forward` is !! `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of `forward`. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the same second-order tensor expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call quat_shiftmat ( q , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor2 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_shift_tensor3 ( a , q , forward , ashift ) !! Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by a unit quaternion `q`. !! This orientation is used for both transformation directions.  The tensor !! remains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a different frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! Components of a third-order tensor.  Expressed in A if `forward` is !! `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion expressed in A, regardless of `forward`. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the same third-order tensor expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call quat_shiftmat ( q , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor3 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_to_aa ( q , axis , angle ) !! Converts a unit quaternion to an *axis-angle* representation. An !! identity quaternion will return [1,0,0] as the axis. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis of rotation. real ( rp ), intent ( out ) :: angle !! Angle in radian (lies in `[0, pi]`). real ( rp ) :: p ( 3 ), q_ ( 4 ), r , s q_ = q if ( q_ ( 1 ) < 0.0_rp ) q_ = - q_ s = maxval ( abs ( q_ ( 2 : 4 ) ) ) if ( s == 0.0_rp ) then ! Identity rotation (angle = 0) axis ( 1 ) = 1.0_rp ; axis ( 2 ) = 0.0_rp ; axis ( 3 ) = 0.0_rp angle = 0.0_rp else ! Usual case p = q_ ( 2 : 4 ) / s r = norm ( p ) axis = p / r angle = 2.0_rp * atan2 ( s * r , q_ ( 1 )) end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_to_dcm ( q , dcm ) !! Converts a unit quaternion to a direction cosine matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. call quat_shiftmat ( q , . true ., dcm ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine quat_to_euler ( q , seq , world , tol , euler ) !! Converts a unit quaternion to an Euler angle sequence. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( in ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler !! Euler angles. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call quat_rotmat ( q , rotmat ) call factor_rotmat ( rotmat , seq , world , tol , euler ) end subroutine !*****************************************************************************! !                                  AXIS ANGLE                                 ! !*****************************************************************************! subroutine aa_fix ( axis , angle , normalize_axis , estat ) !! For a given orientation in *axis-angle* representation, returns a !! modified `axis` and `angle` to ensure that `angle` lies in `[0, pi]` !! while preserving the rotation. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in out ) :: axis !! Axis of rotation. On entry, must be a non-zero vector. On return, !! if `normalize_axis=.true.`, the normalized `axis`. !! If `normalize_axis=.false.`, it has the same magnitude as `axis` !! and may need to be normalized before using other axis-angle functions. real ( rp ), intent ( in out ) :: angle !! On entry, angle in radian. On return, modified angle in radian !! within `[0, pi]`. logical , intent ( in ) :: normalize_axis !! Whether to normalize the axis to a unit vector. integer , intent ( out ) :: estat !! Error code. Equals `1` if `axis` is a zero vector, else `0`. estat = 0 ! Check if axis is a zero vector if (( axis ( 1 ) == 0.0_rp ) . and . ( axis ( 2 ) == 0.0_rp ) . and . ( axis ( 3 ) == 0.0_rp )) then estat = 1 ; return end if if ( normalize_axis ) call normalized ( axis , estat ) if ( estat == 1 ) return ! Get principal signed angle in [-pi, pi] angle = atan2 ( sin ( angle ), cos ( angle )) ! Make the angle non-negative if ( angle < 0.0_rp ) then angle = - angle axis = - axis end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_rand ( axis , angle ) !! Generates a random orientation in *axis-angle* representation drawn from !! a uniform distribution on the space of rotations in 3D. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: axis real ( rp ), intent ( out ) :: angle real ( rp ) :: q ( 4 ) call quat_rand ( q ) call quat_to_aa ( q , axis , angle ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_rotmat ( axis , angle , rotmat ) !! Returns the matrix for an active rotation about `axis` through `angle`, !! with positive angles following the right-hand rule. !! !! For a column vector `v` of length 3, the rotated vector `v' = R v`, where !! `R` is the returned matrix. The components of `v`, `v'`, and `axis` are !! expressed in the same fixed orthonormal basis. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand !! rule. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat !! Rotation matrix. real ( rp ) :: sine , sine_2 , cosine , icos sine = sin ( angle ) cosine = cos ( angle ) sine_2 = sin ( angle / 2.0_rp ) icos = 2.0_rp * sine_2 * sine_2 ! equals (1 - cosine) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = axis ( 1 ) * axis ( 1 ) * icos + cosine rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = axis ( 1 ) * axis ( 2 ) * icos + axis ( 3 ) * sine rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = axis ( 3 ) * axis ( 1 ) * icos - axis ( 2 ) * sine rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = axis ( 1 ) * axis ( 2 ) * icos - axis ( 3 ) * sine rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = axis ( 2 ) * axis ( 2 ) * icos + cosine rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = axis ( 2 ) * axis ( 3 ) * icos + axis ( 1 ) * sine rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = axis ( 1 ) * axis ( 3 ) * icos + axis ( 2 ) * sine rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = axis ( 2 ) * axis ( 3 ) * icos - axis ( 1 ) * sine rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = axis ( 3 ) * axis ( 3 ) * icos + cosine end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_from_rotmat ( rotmat , axis , angle ) !! Extracts axis and angle from a rotation matrix. !! If `rotmat` is an identity matrix, the axis returned is [1,0,0]. If the !! angle is exactly `pi`, either sign of the axis is valid. !! real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat !! Rotation matrix (must be orthonormal with determinant equal to one). real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( out ) :: angle !! Angle of rotation in radian within `[0, pi]`. real ( rp ) :: cos_angle , sin_angle , s , tr , w ( 3 ) integer :: k , estat ! Cos of the angle from the trace tr = rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) + rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) + rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) cos_angle = ( tr - 1.0_rp ) / 2.0_rp ! Clamp cos_angle to [-1, 1] cos_angle = max ( - 1.0_rp , min ( 1.0_rp , cos_angle )) ! Sin of the angle from the anti-symmetric vector w w ( 1 ) = 0.5_rp * ( rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) - rotmat ( 2 , 3 )) w ( 2 ) = 0.5_rp * ( rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) - rotmat ( 3 , 1 )) w ( 3 ) = 0.5_rp * ( rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) - rotmat ( 1 , 2 )) sin_angle = norm ( w ) ! Calculate the angle angle = atan2 ( sin_angle , cos_angle ) if ( cos_angle >= 0.0_rp ) then ! Angle lies in [0, pi/2] if ( sin_angle > 0.0_rp ) then axis = w / sin_angle else ! Angle = 0; axis non-unique angle = 0.0_rp axis = [ 1.0_rp , 0.0_rp , 0.0_rp ] end if else ! Find the largest entry on the diagonal of rotmat k = maxloc ( [ rotmat ( 1 , 1 ), rotmat ( 2 , 2 ), rotmat ( 3 , 3 )], 1 ) select case ( k ) case ( 1 ) axis ( 1 ) = sqrt ( ( rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) - cos_angle ) / ( 1.0_rp - cos_angle ) ) s = 1.0_rp / ( 2.0_rp * ( 1.0_rp - cos_angle ) * axis ( 1 )) axis ( 2 ) = s * ( rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) + rotmat ( 1 , 2 )) axis ( 3 ) = s * ( rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) + rotmat ( 1 , 3 )) case ( 2 ) axis ( 2 ) = sqrt ( ( rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) - cos_angle ) / ( 1.0_rp - cos_angle ) ) s = 1.0_rp / ( 2.0_rp * ( 1.0_rp - cos_angle ) * axis ( 2 )) axis ( 1 ) = s * ( rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) + rotmat ( 2 , 1 )) axis ( 3 ) = s * ( rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) + rotmat ( 2 , 3 )) case ( 3 ) axis ( 3 ) = sqrt ( ( rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) - cos_angle ) / ( 1.0_rp - cos_angle ) ) s = 1.0_rp / ( 2.0_rp * ( 1.0_rp - cos_angle ) * axis ( 3 )) axis ( 1 ) = s * ( rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) + rotmat ( 3 , 1 )) axis ( 2 ) = s * ( rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) + rotmat ( 3 , 2 )) end select end if ! Resolve axis sign if ( dot_product ( axis , w ) < 0.0_rp ) axis = - axis call aa_fix ( axis , angle , . true ., estat ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_rotate_vectors ( v , axis , angle , vrot ) !! Rotates vectors about `axis` by `angle`. !! !! The components of `axis`, `v`, and the rotated vectors are all !! expressed in the same fixed basis. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Vectors to rotate stored as columns. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand !! rule. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vrot !! `(3,n)`. Rotated vectors. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call aa_rotmat ( axis , angle , rotmat ) vrot = matmul ( rotmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_shiftmat ( axis , angle , forward , shiftmat ) !! Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to an *axis-angle* !! representation. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle of rotation in radian. Positive angles follow the right-hand !! rule. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: shiftmat !! Shifter matrix. !Get shiftmat assuming forward == .true. call aa_rotmat ( - axis , angle , shiftmat ) if (. not . forward ) then shiftmat = transpose ( shiftmat ) end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_shift_vectors ( v , axis , angle , forward , vshift ) !! Transform vector components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by `axis` and `angle`, !! with `axis` expressed in A and positive angles following the right-hand !! rule. This orientation is used for both transformation directions. !! The vectors remain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a !! different frame. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Components of a vectors stored as columns. Expressed in !! A if `forward` is `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of `forward` real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians. !! Positive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vshift !! `(3,n)`. Components of the same vectors expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as `v`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call aa_shiftmat ( axis , angle , forward , shiftmat ) vshift = matmul ( shiftmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_shift_tensor2 ( a , axis , angle , forward , ashift ) !! Transforms second-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by `axis` and `angle`, !! with `axis` expressed in A and positive angles following the right-hand !! rule. This orientation is used for both transformation directions. !! The tensor remains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a !! different frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! Components of a second-order tensor, expressed in A if `forward` is !! `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of `forward` real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians. !! Positive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the second-order tensor expressed in B if `forward` is !! `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call aa_shiftmat ( axis , angle , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor2 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_shift_tensor3 ( a , axis , angle , forward , ashift ) !! Transforms third-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by `axis` and `angle`, !! with `axis` expressed in A and positive angles following the right-hand !! rule. This orientation is used for both transformation directions. !! The tensor remains unchanged; only its components are expressed in a !! different frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! Components of a third-order tensor, expressed in A if `forward` is !! `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis expressed in A, regardless of `forward` real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle specifying the orientation of B relative to A, in radians. !! Positive angles follow the right-hand rule. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the third-order tensor expressed in B if `forward` is !! `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call aa_shiftmat ( axis , angle , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor3 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_to_quat ( axis , angle , q ) !! Converts an *axis-angle* representation to a unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle of rotation in radian. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: q !! Unit quaternion in the canonical form. q ( 1 ) = cos ( 0.5_rp * angle ) q ( 2 : 4 ) = sin ( 0.5_rp * angle ) * axis !Normalize to ensure unit quaternion and canonicalize call quat_normalized ( q , . true .) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_to_dcm ( axis , angle , dcm ) !! Converts an *axis-angle* representation to a direction cosine matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along  the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle of rotation in radian. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. call aa_shiftmat ( axis , angle , . true ., dcm ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine aa_to_euler ( axis , angle , seq , world , tol , euler ) !! Coverts an *axis-angle* representation to *Euler angles*. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! Angle in radian. character ( len = 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler !! Euler angles. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call aa_rotmat ( axis , angle , rotmat ) call factor_rotmat ( rotmat , seq , world , tol , euler ) end subroutine !*****************************************************************************! !                           DIRECTION COSINE MATRIX                           ! !*****************************************************************************! logical function mat_is_dcm ( mat , tol ) !! Checks if `mat` is a direction cosine matrix or not. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: mat !! Matrix to check. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Absolute tolerance for comparing determinant and orthogonality. mat_is_dcm = mat_is_rotmat ( mat , tol ) end function !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_from_frames ( A , B , dcm ) !! Returns the direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A, !! where the bases of the frames are resolved in an underlying fixed frame F. !! If F coincides with A, then `A` reduces to an identity matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: A !! The columns of A represent the orthonormal basis vectors of a !! right-handed frame A resolved in F. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: B !! The columns of B represent the orthonormal basis vectors of a !! right-handed frame B resolved in F. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A dcm = matmul ( transpose ( B ), A ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_rotmat ( dcm , rotmat ) !! Returns the rotation matrix corresponding to a direction cosine matrix. !! !! Let D be the direction cosine matrix of frame B relative to frame A.  The !! rotation matrix R corresponding to D rotates vectors resolved in A such !! that the bases of A align with those of B, when all the bases are resolved !! in A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat !! Rotation matrix. rotmat = transpose ( dcm ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_shiftmat ( dcm , forward , shiftmat ) !! Returns the shifter matrix corresponding to a direction cosine matrix. !! !! Let D be the direction cosine matrix of frame B relative to frame A. The !! shifter matrix S corresponding to D transforms components of vectors (or !! tensors) resolved in A to those in B (or vice-versa). real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: shiftmat !! Shifter matrix. if ( forward ) then shiftmat = dcm else shiftmat = transpose ( dcm ) end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_rotate_vectors ( v , dcm , vrot ) !! Rotates vectors by a direction cosine matrix. !! !! Let D be the direction cosine matrix of frame B relative to frame A. !! Vectors resolved in A are rotated such that the bases of A align with those !! of B, when all the bases are resolved in A. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Components of a single vector or n vectors stored as columns. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vrot !! `(3,n)`. Rotated vectors. real ( rp ) :: rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) call dcm_rotmat ( dcm , rotmat ) vrot = matmul ( rotmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_shift_vectors ( v , dcm , forward , vshift ) !! Transform vector components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by `dcm`. This orientation !! is used for both transformation directions. The vectors remain unchanged; !! only their components are expressed in a different frame. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed !! in A if `forward` is `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vshift !! `(3,n)`. Components of the same vectors expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as `v`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call dcm_shiftmat ( dcm , forward , shiftmat ) vshift = matmul ( shiftmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_shift_tensor2 ( a , dcm , forward , ashift ) !! Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by `dcm`. This orientation !! is used for both transformation directions. The tensor remains unchanged; !! only its components are expressed in a different frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! A second-order tensor, resolved in A if `forward` is `.true.`, !! or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the same tensor expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call dcm_shiftmat ( dcm , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor2 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_shift_tensor3 ( a , dcm , forward , ashift ) !! Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by `dcm`. This orientation !! is used for both transformation directions. The tensor remains unchanged; !! only its components are expressed in a different frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! A third-order tensor, resolved in A if `forward` is `.true.`, !! or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix of frame B with respect to frame A. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the same tensor expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call dcm_shiftmat ( dcm , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor3 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_to_quat ( dcm , q ) !! Converts a direction cosine matrix to a unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: q !! Unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ) :: axis ( 3 ) real ( rp ) :: angle call dcm_rotmat ( dcm , rotmat ) call aa_from_rotmat ( rotmat , axis , angle ) call aa_to_quat ( axis , angle , q ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_to_aa ( dcm , axis , angle ) !! Converts a direction cosine matrix to an *axis-angle* representation. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis. real ( rp ), intent ( out ) :: angle !! Angle in radian (lies in `[0, pi]`). real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call dcm_rotmat ( dcm , rotmat ) call aa_from_rotmat ( rotmat , axis , angle ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine dcm_to_euler ( dcm , seq , world , tol , euler ) !! Converts a direction cosine matrix to Euler angles. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler !! Euler angles real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call dcm_rotmat ( dcm , rotmat ) call factor_rotmat ( rotmat , seq , world , tol , euler ) end subroutine !*****************************************************************************! !                                 EULER ANGLES                                ! !*****************************************************************************! subroutine euler_rotmat ( euler , seq , world , rotmat ) !! Returns the rotation matrix for a set of Euler angles. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler character ( len = 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat !! Rotation matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ) :: euler_ if (. not . world ) then euler_ = - euler else euler_ = euler end if select case ( seq ) case ( 'XYZ' ) call rotmat_xyz ( euler_ , rotmat ) case ( 'XZY' ) call rotmat_xzy ( euler_ , rotmat ) case ( 'YXZ' ) call rotmat_yxz ( euler_ , rotmat ) case ( 'YZX' ) call rotmat_yzx ( euler_ , rotmat ) case ( 'ZXY' ) call rotmat_zxy ( euler_ , rotmat ) case ( 'ZYX' ) call rotmat_zyx ( euler_ , rotmat ) case default write ( * , * ) 'seq = ' , seq error stop 'seq out of allowed values.' end select if (. not . world ) rotmat = transpose ( rotmat ) end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine euler_shiftmat ( euler , seq , world , forward , shiftmat ) !! Returns the shifter matrix for a set of Euler angles. !! !! The orientation of frame B relative to frame A is specified by a set of !! Euler angles. The shifter matrix S transforms components of vectors (or !! tensors) resolved in A to those in B (or vice-versa). real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: shiftmat !! Shifter matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call euler_rotmat ( euler , seq , world , rotmat ) if ( forward ) then shiftmat = transpose ( rotmat ) else shiftmat = rotmat end if end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_rotate_vectors ( v , euler , seq , world , vrot ) !! Rotates vectors with a set of Euler angles. The components of `v` !! and the rotated vectors are all expressed in the same fixed basis. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Components of vectors stored as columns. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vrot !! `(3,n)`. Rotated vectors. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call euler_rotmat ( euler , seq , world , rotmat ) vrot = matmul ( rotmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_shift_vectors ( v , euler , seq , world , forward , vshift ) !! Transform vector components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by Euler angles. !! This orientation is used for both transformation directions. The vectors !! remain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different !! frame. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: v !! `(3,n)`. Components of vectors stored as columns. Expressed !! in A if `forward` is `.true.`, or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: vshift !! `(3,n)`. Components of the same vectors expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. Has the same shape as `v`. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call euler_shiftmat ( euler , seq , world , forward , shiftmat ) vshift = matmul ( shiftmat , v ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_shift_tensor2 ( a , euler , seq , world , forward , ashift ) !! Transform second-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by Euler angles. !! This orientation is used for both transformation directions. The vectors !! remain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different !! frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! A second-order tensor, resolved in A if `forward` is `.true.`, !! or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the same tensor expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call euler_shiftmat ( euler , seq , world , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor2 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_shift_tensor3 ( a , euler , seq , world , forward , ashift ) !! Transform third-order tensor components between frames A and B. !! !! The orientation of B relative to A is specified by Euler angles. !! This orientation is used for both transformation directions. The vectors !! remain unchanged; only their components are expressed in a different !! frame. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! A third-order tensor, resolved in A if `forward` is `.true.`, !! or in B otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. logical , intent ( in ) :: forward !! If `.true.`, transform components from A to B. If `.false.`, !! transform components from B to A. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift !! Components of the same tensor expressed in B if !! `forward` is `.true.`, or in A otherwise. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: shiftmat call euler_shiftmat ( euler , seq , world , forward , shiftmat ) call shift_tensor3 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_to_quat ( euler , seq , world , q ) !! Convert Euler angles to a unit quaternion. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), dimension ( 4 ), intent ( out ) :: q !! Unit quaternion in canonical form. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ) :: axis real ( rp ) :: angle call euler_to_aa ( euler , seq , world , axis , angle ) call aa_to_quat ( axis , angle , q ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_to_aa ( euler , seq , world , axis , angle ) !! Convert Euler angles to an *axis-angle* representation. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: axis !! Unit vector along the axis of rotation. real ( rp ), intent ( out ) :: angle !! Angle of rotation in radian (lies in `[0, pi]`). real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call euler_rotmat ( euler , seq , world , rotmat ) call aa_from_rotmat ( rotmat , axis , angle ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_to_dcm ( euler , seq , world , dcm ) !! Convert Euler angles to a direction cosine matrix. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: dcm !! Direction cosine matrix. call euler_shiftmat ( euler , seq , world , . true ., dcm ) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine euler_to_euler ( euler , seq , world , to_seq , to_world , tol , to_euler ) !! Convert one set of Euler angles to another. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler !! Euler angles. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Sequence for `euler`. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: to_seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Convert `euler` with sequence `seq` to the sequence `to_seq`. logical , intent ( in ) :: to_world !! Whether the converted euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: to_euler !! Converted Euler angles. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat call euler_rotmat ( euler , seq , world , rotmat ) call factor_rotmat ( rotmat , to_seq , to_world , tol , to_euler ) end subroutine !*****************************************************************************! !                           INTERNAL ROUTINES                                 ! !*****************************************************************************! subroutine factor_rotmat ( rotmat , seq , world , tol , euler ) !! Factorize a rotation matrix to obtain the three Euler angles. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat !! Rotation matrix. character ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: seq !! `'XYZ'` | `'XZY'` | `'YXZ'` | `'YZX'` | `'ZXY'` | `'ZYX'`. !! Euler angle sequence. logical , intent ( in ) :: world !! Whether the Euler angles are with respect to the *world* frame or not. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol !! Tolerance (must be >= 0) for setting one outer angle to zero. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler !! Euler angles. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rotmat_ if (. not . world ) then rotmat_ = transpose ( rotmat ) else rotmat_ = rotmat end if select case ( seq ) case ( 'XYZ' ) call factor_rotmat_xyz ( rotmat_ , tol , euler ) case ( 'XZY' ) call factor_rotmat_xzy ( rotmat_ , tol , euler ) case ( 'YXZ' ) call factor_rotmat_yxz ( rotmat_ , tol , euler ) case ( 'YZX' ) call factor_rotmat_yzx ( rotmat_ , tol , euler ) case ( 'ZXY' ) call factor_rotmat_zxy ( rotmat_ , tol , euler ) case ( 'ZYX' ) call factor_rotmat_zyx ( rotmat_ , tol , euler ) case default write ( * , * ) 'seq = ' , seq error stop 'seq out of allowed values.' end select if (. not . world ) euler = - euler end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine shift_tensor2 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) !! Shifts a second order tensor, i.e. `(3,3)` matrix using a shifter matrix real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: shiftmat real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift ashift = matmul ( shiftmat , matmul ( a , transpose ( shiftmat ))) end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine shift_tensor3 ( a , shiftmat , ashift ) !! Shifts a third order tensor, i.e. `(3,3,3)` matrix using a shifter matrix real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: shiftmat real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ashift integer :: i , j , k , p , q , r ashift = 0.0_rp do r = 1 , 3 do q = 1 , 3 do p = 1 , 3 do k = 1 , 3 do j = 1 , 3 do i = 1 , 3 ashift ( i , j , k ) = ashift ( i , j , k ) + & shiftmat ( i , p ) * shiftmat ( j , q ) * shiftmat ( k , r ) * a ( p , q , r ) end do end do end do end do end do end do end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine rotmat_xyz ( euler , rotmat ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: sin_phi , sin_theta , sin_psi real ( rp ) :: cos_phi , cos_theta , cos_psi rotmat = 0.0_rp phi = euler ( 1 ); theta = euler ( 2 ); psi = euler ( 3 ) sin_phi = sin ( phi ); sin_theta = sin ( theta ); sin_psi = sin ( psi ) cos_phi = cos ( phi ); cos_theta = cos ( theta ); cos_psi = cos ( psi ) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = cos_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = - sin_theta rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = sin_phi * sin_theta * cos_psi - cos_phi * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = sin_psi * sin_theta * sin_phi + cos_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = sin_phi * cos_theta rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = cos_phi * sin_theta * cos_psi + sin_phi * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = cos_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi - sin_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = cos_phi * cos_theta end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine rotmat_xzy ( euler , rotmat ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: sin_phi , sin_theta , sin_psi real ( rp ) :: cos_phi , cos_theta , cos_psi rotmat = 0.0_rp phi = euler ( 1 ); theta = euler ( 2 ); psi = euler ( 3 ) sin_phi = sin ( phi ); sin_theta = sin ( theta ); sin_psi = sin ( psi ) cos_phi = cos ( phi ); cos_theta = cos ( theta ); cos_psi = cos ( psi ) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = cos_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = sin_psi rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = - sin_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = sin_phi * sin_theta - cos_phi * cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = cos_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = sin_phi * cos_theta + cos_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = cos_phi * sin_theta + sin_phi * cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = - sin_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = cos_phi * cos_theta - sin_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine rotmat_yxz ( euler , rotmat ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: sin_phi , sin_theta , sin_psi real ( rp ) :: cos_phi , cos_theta , cos_psi rotmat = 0.0_rp phi = euler ( 1 ); theta = euler ( 2 ); psi = euler ( 3 ) sin_phi = sin ( phi ); sin_theta = sin ( theta ); sin_psi = sin ( psi ) cos_phi = cos ( phi ); cos_theta = cos ( theta ); cos_psi = cos ( psi ) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = cos_theta * cos_psi - sin_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = sin_phi * sin_theta * cos_psi + cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = - cos_phi * sin_theta rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = - cos_phi * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = cos_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = sin_phi rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = sin_theta * cos_psi + sin_phi * cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = sin_theta * sin_psi - sin_phi * cos_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = cos_phi * cos_theta end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine rotmat_yzx ( euler , rotmat ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: sin_phi , sin_theta , sin_psi real ( rp ) :: cos_phi , cos_theta , cos_psi rotmat = 0.0_rp phi = euler ( 1 ); theta = euler ( 2 ); psi = euler ( 3 ) sin_phi = sin ( phi ); sin_theta = sin ( theta ); sin_psi = sin ( psi ) cos_phi = cos ( phi ); cos_theta = cos ( theta ); cos_psi = cos ( psi ) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = cos_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = sin_phi * sin_theta + cos_phi * cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = sin_phi * cos_theta * sin_psi - cos_phi * sin_theta rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = - sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = cos_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = sin_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = sin_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = cos_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi - sin_phi * cos_theta rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = sin_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi + cos_phi * cos_theta end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine rotmat_zxy ( euler , rotmat ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: sin_phi , sin_theta , sin_psi real ( rp ) :: cos_phi , cos_theta , cos_psi rotmat = 0.0_rp phi = euler ( 1 ); theta = euler ( 2 ); psi = euler ( 3 ) sin_phi = sin ( phi ); sin_theta = sin ( theta ); sin_psi = sin ( psi ) cos_phi = cos ( phi ); cos_theta = cos ( theta ); cos_psi = cos ( psi ) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = cos_theta * cos_psi + sin_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = cos_phi * sin_psi rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = sin_phi * cos_theta * sin_psi - sin_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = sin_phi * sin_theta * cos_psi - cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = cos_phi * cos_psi rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = sin_phi * cos_theta * cos_psi + sin_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = cos_phi * sin_theta rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = - sin_phi rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = cos_phi * cos_theta end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine rotmat_zyx ( euler , rotmat ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: euler real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: rotmat real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: sin_phi , sin_theta , sin_psi real ( rp ) :: cos_phi , cos_theta , cos_psi rotmat = 0.0_rp phi = euler ( 1 ); theta = euler ( 2 ); psi = euler ( 3 ) sin_phi = sin ( phi ); sin_theta = sin ( theta ); sin_psi = sin ( psi ) cos_phi = cos ( phi ); cos_theta = cos ( theta ); cos_psi = cos ( psi ) rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) = cos_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) = sin_phi * sin_theta * cos_psi + cos_phi * sin_psi rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) = sin_phi * sin_psi - cos_phi * sin_theta * cos_psi rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) = - cos_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) = cos_phi * cos_psi - sin_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) = sin_phi * cos_psi + cos_phi * sin_theta * sin_psi rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) = sin_theta rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) = - sin_phi * cos_theta rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) = cos_phi * cos_theta end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine factor_rotmat_xyz ( rotmat , tol , euler ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: c , s , sphi , cphi ! Recover the middle angle theta s = - rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) c = hypot ( rotmat ( 1 , 1 ), rotmat ( 2 , 1 )) ! = abs(cos theta)) theta = atan2 ( s , c ) !Returns in [-pi/2, pi/2] !Calculate phi (accounting for gimbal lock) if ( c > tol ) then phi = atan2 ( rotmat ( 3 , 2 ), rotmat ( 3 , 3 )) else phi = 0.0_rp end if !Calculate psi using phi sphi = sin ( phi ) cphi = cos ( phi ) psi = atan2 ( sphi * rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) - cphi * rotmat ( 1 , 2 ), & cphi * rotmat ( 2 , 2 ) - sphi * rotmat ( 2 , 3 )) euler ( 1 ) = phi ; euler ( 2 ) = theta ; euler ( 3 ) = psi end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine factor_rotmat_xzy ( rotmat , tol , euler ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: c , s , sphi , cphi !Recover angle psi s = rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) c = hypot ( rotmat ( 1 , 1 ), rotmat ( 3 , 1 )) ! = abs(cos psi)) psi = atan2 ( s , c ) !Returns in [-pi/2, pi/2] !Calculate phi (accounting for gimbal lock) if ( c > tol ) then phi = atan2 ( - rotmat ( 2 , 3 ), rotmat ( 2 , 2 )) else phi = 0.0_rp end if !Calculate theta using phi sphi = sin ( phi ) cphi = cos ( phi ) theta = atan2 ( sphi * rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) + cphi * rotmat ( 1 , 3 ), & sphi * rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) + cphi * rotmat ( 3 , 3 )) euler ( 1 ) = phi ; euler ( 2 ) = theta ; euler ( 3 ) = psi end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine factor_rotmat_yxz ( rotmat , tol , euler ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: c , s , stheta , ctheta !Recover middle angle phi s = rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) c = hypot ( rotmat ( 1 , 2 ), rotmat ( 2 , 2 )) ! = abs(cos phi)) phi = atan2 ( s , c ) !Returns in [-pi/2, pi/2] !Calculate theta (accounting for gimbal lock) if ( c > tol ) then theta = atan2 ( - rotmat ( 3 , 1 ), rotmat ( 3 , 3 )) else theta = 0.0_rp end if !Calculate psi using theta stheta = sin ( theta ) ctheta = cos ( theta ) psi = atan2 ( ctheta * rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) + stheta * rotmat ( 2 , 3 ), & ctheta * rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) + stheta * rotmat ( 1 , 3 )) euler ( 1 ) = phi ; euler ( 2 ) = theta ; euler ( 3 ) = psi end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine factor_rotmat_yzx ( rotmat , tol , euler ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: c , s , stheta , ctheta !Recover middle angle psi s = - rotmat ( 1 , 2 ) c = hypot ( rotmat ( 2 , 2 ), rotmat ( 3 , 2 )) ! = abs(cos psi) psi = atan2 ( s , c ) !Returns in [-pi/2, pi/2] !Calculate theta (accounting for gimbal lock) if ( c > tol ) then theta = atan2 ( rotmat ( 1 , 3 ), rotmat ( 1 , 1 )) else theta = 0.0_rp end if !Calculate phi using theta stheta = sin ( theta ) ctheta = cos ( theta ) phi = atan2 ( stheta * rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) - ctheta * rotmat ( 2 , 3 ), & ctheta * rotmat ( 3 , 3 ) - stheta * rotmat ( 3 , 1 )) euler ( 1 ) = phi ; euler ( 2 ) = theta ; euler ( 3 ) = psi end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine factor_rotmat_zxy ( rotmat , tol , euler ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: c , s , spsi , cpsi !Recover middle angle phi s = - rotmat ( 2 , 3 ) c = hypot ( rotmat ( 1 , 3 ), rotmat ( 3 , 3 )) ! = abs(cos phi)) phi = atan2 ( s , c ) !Returns in [-pi/2, pi/2] !Calculate psi (accounting for gimbal lock) if ( c > tol ) then psi = atan2 ( rotmat ( 2 , 1 ), rotmat ( 2 , 2 )) else psi = 0.0_rp end if !Calculate theta using psi spsi = sin ( psi ) cpsi = cos ( psi ) theta = atan2 ( spsi * rotmat ( 3 , 2 ) - cpsi * rotmat ( 3 , 1 ), & cpsi * rotmat ( 1 , 1 ) - spsi * rotmat ( 1 , 2 )) euler ( 1 ) = phi ; euler ( 2 ) = theta ; euler ( 3 ) = psi end subroutine !******************************************************************************* subroutine factor_rotmat_zyx ( rotmat , tol , euler ) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: rotmat real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: tol real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: euler real ( rp ) :: phi , theta , psi real ( rp ) :: c , s , spsi , cpsi ! Recover the middle angle theta s = rotmat ( 1 , 3 ) c = hypot ( rotmat ( 2 , 3 ), rotmat ( 3 , 3 )) ! = abs(cos theta)) theta = atan2 ( s , c ) !Returns in [-pi/2, pi/2] !Calculate psi (accounting for gimbal lock) if ( c > tol ) then psi = atan2 ( - rotmat ( 1 , 2 ), rotmat ( 1 , 1 )) else psi = 0.0_rp end if !Calculate phi using psi spsi = sin ( psi ) cpsi = cos ( psi ) phi = atan2 ( spsi * rotmat ( 3 , 1 ) + cpsi * rotmat ( 3 , 2 ), & spsi * rotmat ( 2 , 1 ) + cpsi * rotmat ( 2 , 2 )) euler ( 1 ) = phi ; euler ( 2 ) = theta ; euler ( 3 ) = psi end subroutine !****************************************************************************** end module rotlib_m","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rotlib_m.f90.html"},{"title":"utils_math_m.f90 – rotlib","text":"Source Code !********************************************************************************! !                                                                                ! ! The MIT License (MIT)                                                          ! !                                                                                ! ! Copyright (c) 2020 Sarit Dutta                                                 ! !                                                                                ! ! Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy   ! ! of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal  ! ! in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights   ! ! to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell      ! ! copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is          ! ! furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:                       ! !                                                                                ! ! The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all ! ! copies or substantial portions of the Software.                                ! !                                                                                ! ! THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR     ! ! IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,       ! ! FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE    ! ! AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER         ! ! LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,  ! ! OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE  ! ! SOFTWARE.                                                                      ! !                                                                                ! !********************************************************************************! module utils_math_m !! Various utility functions, particularly for use with small matrices. use , intrinsic :: ieee_arithmetic , only : ieee_is_nan , ieee_is_finite use constants_m implicit none interface allclose !! Checks if two arrays are elementwise close within tolerance module procedure allclose_rank1 module procedure allclose_rank2 module procedure allclose_rank3 end interface interface swap !! Swaps two arrays module procedure swap_integer module procedure swap_real module procedure swap_complex end interface swap contains !****************************************************************************** elemental subroutine swap_integer ( a , b ) integer , intent ( in out ) :: a integer , intent ( in out ) :: b integer :: temp temp = a a = b b = temp end subroutine elemental subroutine swap_real ( a , b ) real ( rp ), intent ( in out ) :: a real ( rp ), intent ( in out ) :: b real ( rp ) :: temp temp = a a = b b = temp end subroutine elemental subroutine swap_complex ( a , b ) complex ( rp ), intent ( in out ) :: a complex ( rp ), intent ( in out ) :: b complex ( rp ) :: temp temp = a a = b b = temp end subroutine !****************************************************************************** elemental logical function isclose ( a , b , rel_tol , abs_tol ) !! Checks if two floating point numbers of type double are close within !! tolerance. !! !! Based on python implementation at !! <https://github.com/PythonCHB/close_pep/blob/master/is_close.py>. !! The `method='weak'` option is used here. !\"\" real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: b real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: rel_tol !! Relative tolerance, `rel_tol >= 0`, default 1e-10 real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: abs_tol !! Absolute tolerance, `abs_tol >= 0`, default 0.0 real ( rp ) :: rel_tol_ real ( rp ) :: abs_tol_ real ( rp ) :: diff rel_tol_ = 1e-10_rp abs_tol_ = 0.0_rp if ( present ( rel_tol )) rel_tol_ = rel_tol if ( present ( abs_tol )) abs_tol_ = abs_tol if ( a == b ) then ! short-circuit exact equality isclose = . true . return end if if ((. not . ieee_is_finite ( a )) . or . (. not . ieee_is_finite ( b ))) then ! Includes the case of two infinities of opposite sign, or ! one infinity and one finite number. Two infinities of opposite sign ! would otherwise have an infinite relative tolerance. isclose = . false . return end if diff = abs ( b - a ) isclose = ( (( diff <= abs ( rel_tol_ * b )) . or . ( diff <= abs ( rel_tol_ * a ))) & . or . ( diff <= abs_tol_ ) ) end function !****************************************************************************** logical function allclose_rank1 ( a , b , rel_tol , abs_tol ) !! Checks if two rank-1 floating point arrays of type double are close within !! tolerance. !\"\" real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: a !! `(m,)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: b !! `(m,)` array real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: rel_tol !! Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: abs_tol !! Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 real ( rp ) :: abs_tol_ , rel_tol_ rel_tol_ = 1e-10_rp abs_tol_ = 0.0_rp if ( present ( rel_tol )) rel_tol_ = rel_tol if ( present ( abs_tol )) abs_tol_ = abs_tol allclose_rank1 = all ( isclose ( a , b , rel_tol_ , abs_tol_ )) end function logical function allclose_rank2 ( a , b , rel_tol , abs_tol ) !! Checks if two rank-2 floating point arrays of type double are close within !! tolerance. !\"\" real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: a !! `(m,n)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: b !! `(m,n)` array real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: rel_tol !! Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: abs_tol !! Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 real ( rp ) :: abs_tol_ , rel_tol_ rel_tol_ = 1e-10_rp abs_tol_ = 0.0_rp if ( present ( rel_tol )) rel_tol_ = rel_tol if ( present ( abs_tol )) abs_tol_ = abs_tol allclose_rank2 = all ( isclose ( a , b , rel_tol_ , abs_tol_ )) end function logical function allclose_rank3 ( a , b , rel_tol , abs_tol ) !! Checks if two rank-3 floating point arrays of type double are close within !! tolerance. !\"\" real ( rp ), dimension (:,:,:), intent ( in ) :: a !! `(m,n,p)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:,:,:), intent ( in ) :: b !! `(m,n,p)` array real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: rel_tol !! Relative tolerance; default 1e-10 real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: abs_tol !! Absolute tolerance; default 0.0 real ( rp ) :: abs_tol_ , rel_tol_ rel_tol_ = 1e-10_rp abs_tol_ = 0.0_rp if ( present ( rel_tol )) rel_tol_ = rel_tol if ( present ( abs_tol )) abs_tol_ = abs_tol allclose_rank3 = all ( isclose ( a , b , rel_tol_ , abs_tol_ )) end function !************************************************************************ elemental subroutine rad2deg ( rad , deg ) real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: rad real ( rp ), intent ( out ) :: deg deg = ( 18 0.0_rp / math_pi ) * rad end subroutine !************************************************************************ elemental subroutine deg2rad ( deg , rad ) real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: deg real ( rp ), intent ( out ) :: rad rad = ( math_pi / 18 0.0_rp ) * deg end subroutine !****************************************************************************** elemental function sinc ( x ) result ( res ) !! Calculates sin(x)/x elementwise. ! ! At |x|=1e-4, the first omitted term from the Taylor expansion is ! of the order of 1e-18, comfortably below double-precision rounding error ! near 1. real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: x real ( rp ) :: res if ( abs ( x ) < 1e-4_rp ) then res = 1.0_rp - x * x / 6.0_rp else res = sin ( x ) / x end if end function !****************************************************************************** function norm ( v ) result ( res ) !! Calculates the 2-norm of a vector. real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: v real ( rp ) :: res real ( rp ) :: s , snorm , tmp integer :: i ! scaling factor s = 0.0_rp do i = 1 , size ( v ) s = max ( s , abs ( v ( i ))) end do if ( s == 0.0_rp ) then res = 0.0_rp ! norm of a zero vector is zero return end if ! calculate the square of the scaled norm snorm = 0.0_rp tmp = 0.0_rp do i = 1 , size ( v ) tmp = v ( i ) / s snorm = snorm + tmp * tmp end do ! unscale and return res = s * sqrt ( snorm ) end function !****************************************************************************** subroutine normalized ( v , estat ) !! Normalizes a vector in-place. If the magnitude of the vector is zero, !! the vector is not modified and an optional error status of `1` is returned. real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in out ) :: v !! A vector integer , intent ( out ), optional :: estat !! Error status. Equals `1` in case of a zero vector, and `0` otherwise. real ( rp ) :: s , snorm integer :: i ! scaling factor s = 0.0_rp do i = 1 , size ( v ) s = max ( s , abs ( v ( i ))) end do if ( s == 0.0_rp ) then ! cannot normalize a zero vector if ( present ( estat )) estat = 1 return end if v = v / s ! scale the vector snorm = sqrt ( dot_product ( v , v )) ! scaled norm v = v / snorm ! Divide by the scaled norm if ( present ( estat )) estat = 0 ! Set optional error status end subroutine !************************************************************************ subroutine cross ( a , b , c ) !! Calculates the cross product between two 3-element vectors. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: b real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: c !! Cross product of `a` and `b`; **c** = **a** x **b** c ( 1 ) = a ( 2 ) * b ( 3 ) - a ( 3 ) * b ( 2 ) c ( 2 ) = a ( 3 ) * b ( 1 ) - a ( 1 ) * b ( 3 ) c ( 3 ) = a ( 1 ) * b ( 2 ) - a ( 2 ) * b ( 1 ) end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine cross_mat ( a , mat ) !! Calculates the cross product matrix of a 3-element vector. The cross !! product matrix **A** of **a** is defined as **a** x **b** = **A** . **b**, !! where **b** is another 3-element vector. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: mat !! Cross product matrix of `a` mat = 0.0_rp mat ( 2 , 1 ) = a ( 3 ) mat ( 3 , 1 ) = - a ( 2 ) mat ( 1 , 2 ) = - a ( 3 ) mat ( 3 , 2 ) = a ( 1 ) mat ( 1 , 3 ) = a ( 2 ) mat ( 2 , 3 ) = - a ( 1 ) end subroutine !****************************************************************************** function vec_angle_3d ( a , b ) result ( res ) !! Returns the angle (in radian) between two non-zero vectors in 3D. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: b real ( rp ) :: res real ( rp ) :: ab , a_ ( 3 ), b_ ( 3 ), c ( 3 ), c_mag a_ = a / maxval ( abs ( a )) b_ = b / maxval ( abs ( b )) call cross ( a_ , b_ , c ) c_mag = norm ( c ) ab = dot_product ( a_ , b_ ) res = atan2 ( c_mag , ab ) end function !****************************************************************************** function uvec_angle ( u , v ) result ( res ) !! Returns the angle (in radian) between two unit vectors using Kahan's half !! angle formula. real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: u !! Unit vector real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: v !! Unit vector real ( rp ) :: res real ( rp ) :: s_mag , d_mag s_mag = norm ( u + v ) d_mag = norm ( u - v ) res = 2.0_rp * atan2 ( d_mag , s_mag ) end function !****************************************************************************** function scalar_triple_product ( a , b , c ) result ( res ) !! Returns the scalar triple product **a**.(**b** x **c**) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: b real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: c real ( rp ) :: res res = a ( 1 ) * ( b ( 2 ) * c ( 3 ) - c ( 2 ) * b ( 3 ) ) - a ( 2 ) * ( b ( 1 ) * c ( 3 ) - c ( 1 ) * b ( 3 ) ) & + a ( 3 ) * ( b ( 1 ) * c ( 2 ) - c ( 1 ) * b ( 2 ) ) end function !****************************************************************************** subroutine vector_triple_product ( a , b , c , d ) !! Returns the vector triple product **d** = **a** x (**b** x **c**) real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: b real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( in ) :: c real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: d !! Vector triple product d = b * ( a ( 1 ) * c ( 1 ) + a ( 2 ) * c ( 2 ) + a ( 3 ) * c ( 3 ) ) & - c * ( a ( 1 ) * b ( 1 ) + a ( 2 ) * b ( 2 ) + a ( 3 ) * b ( 3 ) ) end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine outer ( a , b , c ) !! Calculates the outer product of two vectors, c_{ij} = a_i  b_j. real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: a !! `(m,)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: b !! `(n,)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: c !! `(m,n)` array; Outer product integer :: m , n integer :: i , j m = size ( a ) n = size ( b ) do j = 1 , n do i = 1 , m c ( i , j ) = a ( i ) * b ( j ) end do end do end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine linspace ( start , finish , num , val , step ) !! Generates evenly spaced numbers over a specified interval. Both end !! points are included. If `start` > `finish`, the returned step size (if !! `step` is present) will be negative. !! !! Values are interpolated directly from the endpoints to avoid overflow !! in the endpoint difference. Floating-point rounding can make adjacent !! spacings unequal or produce repeated values. The supplied endpoints !! are assigned exactly. !\"\" real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: start !! Finite starting point real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: finish !! Finite ending point, `finish /= start` integer , intent ( in ) :: num !! Number of values to generate, `num >= 2` real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in out ) :: val !! `(n,)` array, where `n >= num`. Generated values. Elements beyond !! the first `num` values are left as is. real ( rp ), intent ( out ), optional :: step !! Nominal step size, which may differ from adjacent output spacings !! because of rounding. For `num=2`, its calculation can overflow if !! the endpoint difference is not representable. No step is calculated !! when this argument is absent. real ( rp ) :: intervals , t , difference logical :: opposite_signs integer :: i if ( num < 2 ) then write ( * , * ) '[linspace] `num` must be >= 2' stop end if if ( num > size ( val )) then write ( * , * ) '[linspace] `size(val)` must be >= `num`' stop end if if ( start == finish ) then write ( * , * ) '[linspace] `start` must not be equal to `finish`' stop end if intervals = real ( num - 1 , rp ) opposite_signs = ( start < 0.0_rp . and . finish > 0.0_rp ) . or . & ( start > 0.0_rp . and . finish < 0.0_rp ) val ( 1 ) = start ; val ( num ) = finish if ( opposite_signs ) then if ( present ( step )) then if ( num == 2 ) then step = finish - start else step = finish / intervals - start / intervals end if end if do i = 2 , num - 1 t = real ( i - 1 , rp ) / intervals val ( i ) = ( 1.0_rp - t ) * start + t * finish end do else difference = finish - start if ( present ( step )) step = difference / intervals do i = 2 , num - 1 t = real ( i - 1 , rp ) / intervals val ( i ) = start + t * difference end do end if end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine logspace ( start , finish , num , val , base ) !! Generates numbers spaced evenly on a log scale. !! In linear space, the sequence starts at `base ** start` !! (`base` to the power of `start`) and ends with `base ** finish` !! !! Exponents are generated by `linspace`. Floating-point rounding can !! make adjacent ratios unequal or produce repeated values. The endpoint !! powers are subject to rounding, overflow, and underflow as well. !\"\" real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: start !! Finite starting exponent; `base ** start` is the starting value real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: finish !! Finite ending exponent, `finish /= start`; `base ** finish` !! is the ending value integer , intent ( in ) :: num !! Number of values to generate, `num >= 2` real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in out ) :: val !! `(n,)` array, where `n >= num`. Generated values. Elements beyond !! the first `num` values are left as is. real ( rp ), intent ( in ), optional :: base !! Base of the logspace. Must be finite and positive, default is 10. real ( rp ) :: base_ integer :: i if ( num < 2 ) then write ( * , * ) 'logspace `num` must be >= 2' stop end if if ( num > size ( val )) then write ( * , * ) 'logspace `size(val)` must be >= `num`' stop end if if ( start == finish ) then write ( * , * ) 'logspace `start` must not be equal to `finish`' stop end if base_ = 1 0.0_rp if ( present ( base )) base_ = base call linspace ( start , finish , num , val ) do i = 1 , num val ( i ) = base_ ** val ( i ) end do end subroutine !****************************************************************************** function det ( A ) result ( res ) !! Returns the determinant of an (N x N) matrix, where N = 2, 3, or 4. !! !! Original routine by [David Simpson](http://www.davidgsimpson.com/software.html) !! @note For a general NxN matrix do an LU decomp !\"\" real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: A !! `(N,N)` array, where N = 2, 3, or 4. real ( rp ) :: res integer :: nrows nrows = size ( A , 1 ) if ( nrows == 2 ) then res = A ( 1 , 1 ) * A ( 2 , 2 ) - A ( 1 , 2 ) * A ( 2 , 1 ) else if ( nrows == 3 ) then res = A ( 1 , 1 ) * A ( 2 , 2 ) * A ( 3 , 3 ) - A ( 1 , 1 ) * A ( 2 , 3 ) * A ( 3 , 2 ) & - A ( 1 , 2 ) * A ( 2 , 1 ) * A ( 3 , 3 ) + A ( 1 , 2 ) * A ( 2 , 3 ) * A ( 3 , 1 ) & + A ( 1 , 3 ) * A ( 2 , 1 ) * A ( 3 , 2 ) - A ( 1 , 3 ) * A ( 2 , 2 ) * A ( 3 , 1 ) else if ( nrows == 4 ) then res = A ( 1 , 1 ) * ( A ( 2 , 2 ) * ( A ( 3 , 3 ) * A ( 4 , 4 ) - A ( 3 , 4 ) * A ( 4 , 3 )) & + A ( 2 , 3 ) * ( A ( 3 , 4 ) * A ( 4 , 2 ) - A ( 3 , 2 ) * A ( 4 , 4 )) & + A ( 2 , 4 ) * ( A ( 3 , 2 ) * A ( 4 , 3 ) - A ( 3 , 3 ) * A ( 4 , 2 )) ) & - A ( 1 , 2 ) * ( A ( 2 , 1 ) * ( A ( 3 , 3 ) * A ( 4 , 4 ) - A ( 3 , 4 ) * A ( 4 , 3 )) & + A ( 2 , 3 ) * ( A ( 3 , 4 ) * A ( 4 , 1 ) - A ( 3 , 1 ) * A ( 4 , 4 )) & + A ( 2 , 4 ) * ( A ( 3 , 1 ) * A ( 4 , 3 ) - A ( 3 , 3 ) * A ( 4 , 1 )) ) & + A ( 1 , 3 ) * ( A ( 2 , 1 ) * ( A ( 3 , 2 ) * A ( 4 , 4 ) - A ( 3 , 4 ) * A ( 4 , 2 )) & + A ( 2 , 2 ) * ( A ( 3 , 4 ) * A ( 4 , 1 ) - A ( 3 , 1 ) * A ( 4 , 4 )) & + A ( 2 , 4 ) * ( A ( 3 , 1 ) * A ( 4 , 2 ) - A ( 3 , 2 ) * A ( 4 , 1 )) ) & - A ( 1 , 4 ) * ( A ( 2 , 1 ) * ( A ( 3 , 2 ) * A ( 4 , 3 ) - A ( 3 , 3 ) * A ( 4 , 2 )) & + A ( 2 , 2 ) * ( A ( 3 , 3 ) * A ( 4 , 1 ) - A ( 3 , 1 ) * A ( 4 , 3 )) & + A ( 2 , 3 ) * ( A ( 3 , 1 ) * A ( 4 , 2 ) - A ( 3 , 2 ) * A ( 4 , 1 )) ) else error stop 'Matrix rank must be 2, 3, or 4.' end if end function !****************************************************************************** function trace ( mat ) result ( res ) !! Returns the trace of a square matrix real ( rp ), intent ( in ) :: mat (:,:) !! `(N,N)` array real ( rp ) :: res integer :: nrows integer :: i nrows = size ( mat , 1 ) res = 0.0_rp do i = 1 , nrows res = res + mat ( i , i ) end do end function !****************************************************************************** subroutine identity ( mat_eye ) !! Creates an identity matrix of size n x n. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: mat_eye !! `(n,n)` array integer :: nrows integer :: i nrows = size ( mat_eye , 1 ) mat_eye = 0.0_rp do i = 1 , nrows mat_eye ( i , i ) = 1.0_rp end do end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine get_diagonal ( mat , d ) !! Returns the diagonal elements of a square matrix. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: mat !! `(n,n)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: d !! `(n,)` array; contains the entries of the main diagonal integer :: n integer :: i n = size ( mat , 1 ) do i = 1 , n d ( i ) = mat ( i , i ) end do end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine add_transpose ( mat ) !! Adds a square matrix and its transpose in place: A_{ij} = A_{ij } + A_{ji} real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in out ) :: mat !! `(n,n)` array integer :: n integer :: i integer :: j n = size ( mat , 1 ) !Dealing with the upper triangular part (including diagonal) do j = 1 , n do i = 1 , j mat ( i , j ) = mat ( i , j ) + mat ( j , i ) end do end do !Dealing with the strictly lower triangular part (i.e. excluding diagonal) do j = 1 , ( n - 1 ) do i = ( j + 1 ), n mat ( i , j ) = mat ( j , i ) end do end do end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine subtract_transpose ( mat ) !! Calculates the difference of a square matrix and its transpose in place: !! A_{ij} = A_{ij } - A_{ji} real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in out ) :: mat integer :: n integer :: i integer :: j n = size ( mat , 1 ) !Dealing with the strictly upper triangular part (i.e. excluding diagonal) do j = 2 , n do i = 1 , ( j - 1 ) mat ( i , j ) = mat ( i , j ) - mat ( j , i ) end do end do !Dealing with the strictly lower triangular part (i.e. excluding diagonal) do j = 1 , ( n - 1 ) do i = ( j + 1 ), n mat ( i , j ) = - mat ( j , i ) end do end do !Putting the diagonal to zero do i = 1 , n mat ( i , i ) = 0.0_rp end do end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine multiply_transpose ( A , B ) !! Multiplies a matrix with its transpose: !! \\mathbf{\\mathrm{B}} = \\mathbf{\\mathrm{A}} \\cdot \\mathbf{\\mathrm{A}}&#94;T !\"\" real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: A !! `(m,n)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: B !! `(m,m)` array !A is m x n, A&#94;T is n x m, so B is m x m B = matmul ( A , transpose ( A )) end subroutine !****************************************************************************** function get_quad_form ( A , x ) result ( res ) !! Calculates the quadratic form *x&#94;T A x*, where A is an *n x n* matrix and *x* is a !! vector of length *n* !\"\" real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in ) :: A !! `(n,n)` array real ( rp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! `(n,)` array real ( rp ) :: res integer :: n integer :: i , j n = size ( A , 2 ) res = 0.0_rp do j = 1 , n do i = 1 , n res = res + A ( i , j ) * x ( j ) * x ( i ) end do end do end function !****************************************************************************** subroutine orth_mgs ( a , estat ) !! Orthogonalizes a set of non-zero vectors in-place using modified !! Gram-Schmidt orthonormalization. !! !! *Reference:* Golub and Van Loan, Matrix Computations, 4th edition, !! Section 5.2.8, Algorithm 5.2.6, p. 255. real ( rp ), dimension (:,:), intent ( in out ) :: a !! `(m,n)` rank `n` array, where `m >= n`, storing the vectors !! column-wise. On return, the columns of the matrix are overwritten !! with the orthogonal vectors. integer , intent ( out ) :: estat !! Error code. Returns `1` if during execution a column is found to be !! zero, `0` otherwise. A return with `estat=1` may leave `a` partially !! overwritten. integer :: j , k , n n = size ( a , 2 ) do k = 1 , n call normalized ( a (:, k ), estat ) if ( estat == 1 ) return do j = k + 1 , n a (:, j ) = a (:, j ) - dot_product ( a (:, k ), a (:, j )) * a (:, k ) end do end do end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine invert_mat33 ( a , inv_a ) !! Inverts a 3x3 matrix with non-zero determinant. !! !! *Reference:* https://www.geometrictools.com/Documentation/LaplaceExpansionTheorem.pdf real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! Matrix real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: inv_a !! Matrix inverse real ( rp ) :: as ( 3 , 3 ), det_as , s s = maxval ( abs ( a )) ! scale as = a / s ! scaled a inv_a ( 1 , 1 ) = as ( 2 , 2 ) * as ( 3 , 3 ) - as ( 2 , 3 ) * as ( 3 , 2 ) inv_a ( 2 , 1 ) = - ( as ( 2 , 1 ) * as ( 3 , 3 ) - as ( 2 , 3 ) * as ( 3 , 1 )) inv_a ( 3 , 1 ) = as ( 2 , 1 ) * as ( 3 , 2 ) - as ( 2 , 2 ) * as ( 3 , 1 ) inv_a ( 1 , 2 ) = - ( as ( 1 , 2 ) * as ( 3 , 3 ) - as ( 1 , 3 ) * as ( 3 , 2 )) inv_a ( 2 , 2 ) = as ( 1 , 1 ) * as ( 3 , 3 ) - as ( 1 , 3 ) * as ( 3 , 1 ) inv_a ( 3 , 2 ) = - ( as ( 1 , 1 ) * as ( 3 , 2 ) - as ( 1 , 2 ) * as ( 3 , 1 )) inv_a ( 1 , 3 ) = as ( 1 , 2 ) * as ( 2 , 3 ) - as ( 1 , 3 ) * as ( 2 , 2 ) inv_a ( 2 , 3 ) = - ( as ( 1 , 1 ) * as ( 2 , 3 ) - as ( 1 , 3 ) * as ( 2 , 1 )) inv_a ( 3 , 3 ) = as ( 1 , 1 ) * as ( 2 , 2 ) - as ( 1 , 2 ) * as ( 2 , 1 ) !Determinant of the scaled matrix det_as = as ( 1 , 1 ) * inv_a ( 1 , 1 ) + as ( 1 , 2 ) * inv_a ( 2 , 1 ) + as ( 1 , 3 ) * inv_a ( 3 , 1 ) inv_a = inv_a / det_as ! Unscale inv_a = inv_a / s end subroutine !****************************************************************************** subroutine eigval_33rsym ( a , ev ) !! Calculates the eigenvalues of a finite real symmetric 3 x 3 matrix, !! in decreasing order. The input matrix is not modified. !! !! Uses maximum-entry scaling and Jacobi rotations to avoid overflow in !! intermediate products and cancellation in cubic-equation formulas near !! repeated eigenvalues. Diagonal matrices are handled directly. !! Iteration stops when the largest off-diagonal entry is at most machine !! epsilon times the largest absolute diagonal entry of the scaled matrix. !! !! Accuracy is relative to the matrix scale; high relative accuracy for !! very small eigenvalues or very small eigenvalue gaps is not guaranteed. !! Rescaling can overflow if an eigenvalue is outside the range of `rp`, !! or underflow if it is too small to represent. !! !! *Reference:* J. Kopp, Efficient numerical diagonalization of Hermitian !! 3 x 3 matrices, https://arxiv.org/abs/physics/0610206 real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( in ) :: a !! Finite symmetric input matrix. Both triangles must be supplied. real ( rp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: ev !! Eigenvalues, with `ev(1) >= ev(2) >= ev(3)`. real ( rp ) :: b ( 3 , 3 ), scale , off , diagonal_scale real ( rp ) :: delta , tangent , cosine , sine , x , y integer :: p , q , k if ( a ( 1 , 2 ) == 0.0_rp . and . a ( 1 , 3 ) == 0.0_rp . and . & a ( 2 , 3 ) == 0.0_rp ) then ! Preserve diagonal entries exactly, including the zero matrix. ev = [ a ( 1 , 1 ), a ( 2 , 2 ), a ( 3 , 3 )] else scale = maxval ( abs ( a )) b = a / scale do ! Annihilate the largest off-diagonal entry. p = 1 ; q = 2 if ( abs ( b ( 1 , 3 )) > abs ( b ( p , q ))) then p = 1 ; q = 3 end if if ( abs ( b ( 2 , 3 )) > abs ( b ( p , q ))) then p = 2 ; q = 3 end if off = b ( p , q ) diagonal_scale = max ( abs ( b ( 1 , 1 )), abs ( b ( 2 , 2 )), abs ( b ( 3 , 3 ))) if ( abs ( off ) <= epsilon ( 1.0_rp ) * diagonal_scale ) exit ! Stable rotation tangent with magnitude at most one. Avoid ! dividing the diagonal difference by a possibly tiny off-diagonal. delta = 0.5_rp * ( b ( q , q ) - b ( p , p )) tangent = off / ( delta + sign ( hypot ( delta , off ), delta )) cosine = 1.0_rp / sqrt ( 1.0_rp + tangent * tangent ) sine = tangent * cosine b ( p , p ) = b ( p , p ) - tangent * off b ( q , q ) = b ( q , q ) + tangent * off b ( p , q ) = 0.0_rp ; b ( q , p ) = 0.0_rp k = 6 - p - q ! The remaining row/column index. x = b ( k , p ); y = b ( k , q ) b ( k , p ) = cosine * x - sine * y b ( p , k ) = b ( k , p ) b ( k , q ) = sine * x + cosine * y b ( q , k ) = b ( k , q ) end do ev = [ b ( 1 , 1 ), b ( 2 , 2 ), b ( 3 , 3 )] * scale end if if ( ev ( 1 ) < ev ( 2 )) call swap ( ev ( 1 ), ev ( 2 )) if ( ev ( 1 ) < ev ( 3 )) call swap ( ev ( 1 ), ev ( 3 )) if ( ev ( 2 ) < ev ( 3 )) call swap ( ev ( 2 ), ev ( 3 )) end subroutine !****************************************************************************** end module utils_math_m","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/utils_math_m.f90.html"},{"title":"User Guide – rotlib","text":"Conventions Active and passive rotations In the following, all functions dealing with rotations perform active rotations following the right-hand rule. E.g., aa_rotate_vectors actively\nrotates vectors about an axis through an angle in a given frame. Passive rotation operations are referred to as shifting . They are performed\nusing a shifter matrix. Conceptually, these can be thought of as transforming\n(or shifting) the components of a fixed vector (or tensor) from one frame to\nanother. E.g. aa_shift_vectors transforms the components of a set of\nvectors from frame A to frame B, where frame B is obtained by rotating frame A\nabout an axis through an angle and the set of vectors as well as the axis are\nresolved in frame A. The transformation from A to B is referred to as the forward direction, whereas that from B to A is called the reverse direction. Note that the axis is resolved in frame A irrespective of the\ndirection. Quaternions Quaternions are represented by a vector of four elements, where the first\nelement represents the scalar part and the latter three represent the\nvector part. Thus, assuming 0-based indexing, q = q[0] + q[1]*i + q[2]*j + q[3]*k . A unit (or normalized) quaternion, used for representing orientations (or\nrotations) in 3-space is a quaternion whose magnitude is unity. It is related\nto a 3-D rotation about an axis u through an angle theta via the\nfollowing relations (assuming 0-based indexing): q[0] = cos(theta/2)\nq[1] = u[0] * sin(theta/2)\nq[2] = u[1] * sin(theta/2)\nq[3] = u[2] * sin(theta/2) In the canonical form, the first non-zero element of a unit quaternion is\npositive. Multiplication of quaternions and rotations by unit quaternions follow\nHamilton's convention. See, e.g., Kuipers, J. B., Quaternions and Rotation Sequences , 1999, Princeton\n  University Press, Princeton, NJ Hanson, A. J., Visualizing Quaternions , 2006, Morgan Kaufmann Publishers,\n  San Francisco, CA Axis-angle The axis-angle representation consists of a unit vector pointing along the axis\nof rotation and an angle (in radian) of rotation. The rotation follows the\nright-hand rule for positive angles. In the canonical form the angle is\nrestricted to lie in [0, pi]. Direction cosine matrix (DCM) The DCM gives the orientation of a frame B with respect to another frame A, and\ntransforms vector components from A to B. Its entries are the dot products of\nB's basis vectors with A's basis vectors, with both sets expressed in the same\northonormal frame F. Let a_i be the basis vectors of frame A and b_i those\nof frame B resolved in a fixed frame F. The DCM is D_ij = b_i . a_j . In\nmatrix notation, D = B . A&#94;T for row-wise storage of the basis vectors and D = B&#94;T . A assuming column-wise storage. If A and F coincide, then D = B (row-based) or D = B&#94;T (column-based). Euler angles Euler angles are represented as three-element vectors, along with a rotation\nsequence and a boolean flag world specifying the frame of rotation. The\nelements represent rotations about X, Y, and Z, respectively. The order of\nrotations is specified by a separate argument seq . E.g. ea = [phi, theta, psi], seq = 'YZX', world=True indicates a rotation\nby theta along 'Y', followed by another rotation by psi along 'Z', and\nfinally a third rotation about 'X' by phi , where the rotations are with\nrespect to a fixed frame called the world frame. If world=False , the\nrotations are performed with respect to the moving body frame. The following table describes ranges of returned principal representations,\nthey do not restrict angles accepted by the construction functions. Sequence phi theta psi XYZ, ZYX [-pi, pi] [-pi/2, pi/2] [-pi, pi] XZY, YZX [-pi, pi] [-pi, pi] [-pi/2, pi/2] ZXY, YXZ [-pi/2, pi/2] [-pi, pi] [-pi, pi] Functions that extract Euler angles accept a non-negative tolerance parameter tol . In factorizing a rotation matrix near a singularity, if the absolute\nvalue of the cosine of the middle angle is less than or equal to tol , one of\nthe outer angles is set to zero as per the following table. Sequence Angle set to zero XYZ, XZY phi YXZ, YZX theta ZXY, ZYX psi Note that applying the above convention near, but not exactly at a singularity,\ncan introduce reconstruction error of the order of tol ; it is not a\nguaranteed reconstruction-error bound. Reference: D. Eberly, Euler angle formulas .","tags":"","url":"page/index.html"}]}